     "md": "Level 5/unit 2/unit 2.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 2 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nAndrea and her colleague Craig are talking in the break room.\nAndrea: That was the longest presentation ever!\nCraig: Tell me about it! I nodded off **during** Kathy's speech.\nAndrea: Was it that boring?\nCraig: No, I'm just worn out. I have to turn in a budget report **in** two days, and it's a lot of work.\nAndrea: I see. Speaking of budgets, is anyone in accounting here today?\nCraig: Yeah. Jenny will be in the office **until** 3:00. Roger will be gone **for** a while, though.\nAndrea: All right. I'll swing by their office.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. I nodded off during Kathy's speech.\nsmooth: “nodded off”\nNối từ nodded với từ off tiếp theo và đọc liền mạch như một từ.\n\n2. Was it that boring?\nsmooth: “Was it”\nstrong: “that”\nTừ that có nghĩa như là “đến thế hả”. Đọc nhấn mạnh từ that.\n\n3. Jenny will be in the office until 3:00.\nsmooth: “Jenny will be”, “in the office”\n“Jenny will be” đọc liền mạch giống như là “Jenny'll be”. Đọc nhấn mạnh từ office trong cụm in the office.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nGiới từ chỉ thời gian - thời điểm: during\nPlease keep your seat belt fastened [[during]] the flight.\n\nGiới từ chỉ thời gian - thời điểm: for\nI didn't see her [[for]] a long time.\n\nGiới từ chỉ thời gian - thời điểm: until\nI stayed at home [[until]] noon.\n\nGiới từ chỉ thời gian - thời điểm: by\nPlease be ready to go [[by]] six o'clock.\n\nGiới từ chỉ thời gian - thời điểm: in\nWe're going to move to the suburbs of Chicago [[in]] three weeks.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: That was the longest presentation ever!\nB: Tell me about it! I nodded off ________.\nA: Was it that boring?\nB: No, I'm just worn out. I have to turn in a budget report ________, and it's a lot of work.\nA: I see. Speaking of budgets, is anyone in accounting here today?\nB: Yeah. Jenny will be in the office ________. Roger will be gone for a while, though.\nA: All right. I'll swing by their office.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. I nodded off __during Kathy's speech__.\na. during the CEO's report\nb. during the demonstration\nc. during the slide show\n\n2. I have to turn in a budget report __in two days__, and it's a lot of work.\na. in three hours\nb. by the end of the day\nc. by 5:30\n\n3. Jenny will be in the office __until 3:00__.\na. until ten to six\nb. until her clients arrive\nc. until her boss comes back\n",
