     "number": 3,
     "folder": "Level 5/unit 3",
     "md": "Level 5/unit 3/unit 3.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 3 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nCharles and his granddaughter May are chatting on the phone.\nCharles: Hi, May! Nice to hear from you. How's Germany?\nMay: Wonderful. I really **enjoy** liv**ing** in another country. It's a great experience!\nCharles: I bet! Well, how's school going?\nMay: School's going great. Actually, I **wanted to** try for a scholarship ...\nCharles: Oh, is that right?\nMay: Yeah, but in the end I **decided to** come home and look for a job.\nCharles: I see. So when are you coming home?\nMay: Pretty soon. To be honest, I'm really **looking forward to** see**ing** you all again.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. Actually, I wanted to try for a scholarship.\nsmooth: “wanted to”, “for a”\nweak: “for a”\n“Wanted to” và “for a” phát âm liền mạch như là 1 từ.\n\n2. Yeah, but in the end I decided to come home and look for a job.\nsmooth: “but in the end”, “decided to”, “look for a job”\nweak: “in the”, “to”, “for a”\nstrong: “decided”, “come”, “look”\n“Ci” trong decided, come và look đọc mạnh lên.\nIn the, to, for a đọc nhẹ đi.\n\n3. To be honest, I'm really looking forward to seeing you all again.\nsmooth: “To be honest”, “looking forward to”, “seeing you all again”\nweak: “To be”, “to”\nstrong: “really”\nLooking forward to và seeing you all again đọc liền mạch như một từ.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nĐộng từ chỉ có thể theo sau bởi từ to\nI [[want to]] be a soccer player.\nLast summer, Andy [[decided to]] study in Spain.\n\nCụm từ chỉ có thể theo sau bởi V-ing\nI used to [[enjoy]] driv[[ing]] along the coast.\nI [[look forward to]] hear[[ing]] from you.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Hi, May! Nice to hear from you. How's Germany?\nB: Wonderful. I really enjoy ________. It's a great experience!\nA: I bet! Well, how's school going?\nB: School's going great. Actually, I wanted ________ ...\nA: Oh, is that right?\nB: Yeah, but in the end I decided ________.\nA: I see. So when are you coming home?\nB: Pretty soon. To be honest, I'm really looking forward to seeing you all again.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. I really enjoy __living in another country__.\na. learning about a different culture\nb. speaking German every day\nc. talking to people here\n\n2. Actually, I wanted __to try for a scholarship__.\na. to enroll in an advanced course\nb. to apply to an internship program\nc. to take another class over the summer\n\n3. Yeah, but in the end I decided __to come home and look for a job__.\na. to finish my studies this month\nb. to leave Germany at the end of the term\nc. to go sightseeing for a few weeks\n",
