     "name": "unit 7",
     "number": 7,
     "folder": "Level 5/unit 7",
     "md": "Level 5/unit 7/unit 7.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 7 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nAndrea is giving Max directions to a restaurant.\nMax: I'm walking down South Street now.\nAndrea: OK. How many bus stops have you passed?\nMax: Two, I think.\nAndrea: All right. At the next intersection, turn right and walk down the hill. You'll see a tall building on your left.\nMax: OK.\nMax: Oh, there it is!\nAndrea: Great. The restaurant is right beside that building. When you get here, go up the stairs. I'm sitting by the window.\nMax: All right. I'll be there in a minute.\nAndrea: I'll order some appetizers, then. How hungry are you?\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. At the next intersection, turn right and walk down the hill.\nsmooth: “At the next”, “turn right”\nweak: “the”, “intersection”, “right”, “and”\nChữ “t” trong từ intersection gần như không được đọc.\n\n2. The restaurant is right beside that building.\nsmooth: “right beside”\nweak: “The”, “restaurant”, “right”\nstrong: “that”\nBình thường thì từ that sẽ được đọc nhẹ hơn những từ xung quanh. Nhưng trong trường hợp này, that building là từ key word để chỉ nơi cần đến, vậy nên hãy đọc that mạnh hơn.\n\n3. I'll be there in a minute.\nsmooth: “I'll be there”, “in a minute”\n2 cụm từ I'll be there và in a minute được đọc từng cái một liền mạch.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nHow many/much\nHow many/much + N dùng để hỏi về số lượng. How many đi sau là danh từ đếm được, how much đi sau là danh từ không đếm được.\n[[How many]] seats are available now?\n[[How much]] money will you need for the trip?\n\nHow + adj/adv\nHow + adj/adv sử dụng để hỏi về trạng thái của sự vật, hiện tượng.\n[[How far]] is it from here to San Diego?\n[[How soon]] can you be ready?\n\nTừ chỉ phương hướng\nKhi chỉ đường cho người khác, mà sử dụng những từ chỉ phương hướng này sẽ rất tiện lợi.\nturn [[right]] / turn [[left]]\non your [[right]] / on your [[left]]\ngo [[up]] the stairs / go [[down]] the stairs\ngo [[over]] the footbridge\ngo [[past]] the hospital\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: I'm walking down South Street now.\nB: OK. How ________?\nA: Two, I think.\nB: All right. At the next intersection, ________. You'll see a tall building on your left.\nA: OK.\nA: Oh, there it is!\nB: Great. The restaurant is right beside that building. When you get here, go up the stairs. I'm sitting by the window.\nA: All right. I'll be there in a minute.\nB: I'll order some appetizers, then. How ________?\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. How __many bus stops have you passed__?\na. many convenience stores have you seen\nb. many coffee shops have you gone past\nc. many streets have you crossed\n\n2. At the next intersection, __turn right and walk down the hill__.\na. turn left and walk over the bridge\nb. turn right and walk past the train station\nc. turn left and walk two blocks\n\n3. How __hungry are you__?\na. hot do you like your salsa\nb. strong do you like your margarita\nc. many chicken wings do you want\n",
