     "md": "Level 6/unit 2/unit 2.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 2 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nGavin is interviewing Thao for a job at a tour company.\nGavin: Thao, **have** you ever **worked** with international guests?\nThao: Yes, I **have**. I **worked** at a hotel in Hoi An for three years.\nGavin: Great. Here's a tough one. **Have** you ever **made** a big mistake at work?\nThao: Yes, once. Last spring I **booked** the wrong dates for a tour group.\nGavin: Oh no! What did you do?\nThao: I called every hotel in town and found rooms for everyone.\nGavin: That was quick thinking! **Has** anything like that **happened** since?\nThao: No, never. **I've double-checked** every booking since then.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. Have you ever made a big mistake at work?\nweak: “Have you”\nlinking: “made‿a”, “mistake‿at”\nstrong: “ever”, “mistake”, “work”\n“Have” đầu câu hỏi đọc nhẹ /həv/. “made a” nối thành “mây-đơ”, “mistake at” thành “mis-tây-kơt”. Lên giọng ở cuối câu hỏi Yes/No.\n\n2. Last spring I booked the wrong dates for a tour group.\nchange: “booked the” (mất âm t)\nweak: “the”, “for a”\nstrong: “wrong dates”, “tour group”\nĐuôi -ed của “booked” đọc /t/ nhưng gần như mất trước “the”: “búc-đơ”. Âm /t/ của “Last” cũng mất trước “spring”: “las-spring”.\n\n3. I've double-checked every booking since then.\nweak: “I've”\nlinking: “double-checked‿every”\nstrong: “every booking”\nĐuôi -ed sau âm /k/ đọc /t/: checked → “chekt”, rồi nối sang “every”: “chek-te-vri”. “I've” đọc nhẹ nhưng vẫn giữ âm /v/.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“Have” trong câu hỏi đọc nhẹ /həv/; trong câu trả lời ngắn “Yes, I have.” thì đọc mạnh /hæv/.\nĐuôi -ed sau âm vô thanh /k/, /p/, /s/ đọc /t/: booked, checked, helped.\nÂm /t/ kẹp giữa hai phụ âm thường mất: last spring → “las-spring”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Here's a tough one.**\nCâu này hơi khó đây.\nNgười phỏng vấn hay nói câu này trước một câu hỏi khó, để ứng viên chuẩn bị tinh thần.\nCách nói tương đương: Let me ask you a tricky one.\n\n**That was quick thinking!**\nBạn xử lý nhanh thật đấy!\nLời khen khi ai đó nghĩ ra cách giải quyết nhanh trong một tình huống gấp.\nCách nói tương đương: Good thinking!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nHiện tại hoàn thành: kinh nghiệm (Have you ever…?)\nHỏi và kể về trải nghiệm trong đời, không nói thời điểm cụ thể. Trả lời ngắn: Yes, I have. / No, I haven't. “never” = chưa bao giờ.\n[[Have]] you ever [[tried]] durian? – No, I [[haven't]].\nShe [[has]] never [[seen]] snow.\n[[I've met]] his parents a few times.\n\nQuá khứ đơn: khi có thời điểm cụ thể\nKhi nói rõ lúc nào (last year, in May, two days ago) hoặc kể chi tiết chuyện đã xảy ra, phải chuyển sang quá khứ đơn.\n[[I've been]] to Hue. I [[went]] there last summer.\nHe [[started]] this job two months [[ago]].\nWhen [[did]] you [[finish]] college?\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Thao, have you ever worked with international guests?\nB: Yes, I have. I worked ________ for three years.\nA: Great. Here's a tough one. Have you ever made a big mistake at work?\nB: Yes, once. Last spring I ________ for a tour group.\nA: Oh no! What did you do?\nB: I called every hotel in town and found rooms for everyone.\nA: That was quick thinking! Has anything like that happened since?\nB: No, never. I've ________ since then.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. I worked __at a hotel in Hoi An__ for three years.\na. at a beach resort\nb. for a tour company\nc. on a cruise ship\n\n2. Last spring I __booked the wrong dates__ for a tour group.\na. lost the bus tickets\nb. forgot to book lunch\nc. mixed up the rooms\n\n3. I've __double-checked every booking__ since then.\na. been much more careful\nb. checked everything twice\nc. used a checklist\n",
