     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 3 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nHieu is showing his friend Nora the Saigon neighborhood where he grew up.\nHieu: This is it! I **used to** live in that yellow house.\nNora: So cute! **Did** you **use to** play here as a kid?\nHieu: All the time. We **used to** play soccer until dark.\nNora: Not me. I **didn't use to** go outside much. I was such a bookworm.\nHieu: Why am I not surprised? Hey, see that phone shop?\nNora: What **did** it **use to** be?\nHieu: A noodle stall. My grandma **used to** take me there every Sunday.\nNora: That's so sweet. My grandpa **used to** make me pancakes.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. I used to live in that yellow house.\nchange: “used to” (âm d câm)\nlinking: “live‿in”\nstrong: “yellow house”\n“used to” đọc /ˈjuːstə/ “yus-tơ”: chữ “s” đọc /s/ chứ không phải /z/, âm /d/ không đọc. “live in” nối thành “li-vin”.\n\n2. Did you use to play here as a kid?\nchange: “Did‿you” (d + y → j)\nlinking: “as‿a‿kid”\nstrong: “play”, “kid”\n“Did you” nối thành “đi-jơ”. “use to” đọc giống hệt “used to”: “yus-tơ”. “as a kid” đọc liền: “ơ-zơ-kid”. Lên giọng ở cuối câu.\n\n3. I was such a bookworm.\nweak: “was”\nlinking: “such‿a”\nstrong: “bookworm”\n“was” đọc nhẹ /wəz/. “such a” nối thành “sơ-chơ”. Nhấn âm đầu của “bookworm”: BOOK-worm, phần “worm” đọc /wɝːm/ “wơrm”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“used to” và “use to” đọc giống nhau: /ˈjuːstə/ “yus-tơ”.\nĐừng nhầm với động từ “use” (dùng) có âm /z/: I use my phone → /juːz/.\nÂm /d/ gặp “you” biến thành “j”: did you → “đi-jơ”.\nKhi kể chuyện ngày xưa, nhấn vào hoạt động: we used to PLAY SOCCER.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I was such a bookworm.**\nHồi đó mình đúng là con mọt sách.\n“bookworm” (mọt sách) là người rất mê đọc sách. “such a + danh từ” dùng để nhấn mạnh.\nCách nói tương đương: I always had my nose in a book.\n\n**Why am I not surprised?**\nSao mình chẳng thấy bất ngờ gì nhỉ?\nCâu trêu đùa, ý là “chuyện đó đúng như mình đoán”. Đọc với giọng hài hước.\nCách nói tương đương: That doesn't surprise me at all.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nused to + V: thói quen, tình trạng trong quá khứ\nViệc ngày xưa thường làm hoặc điều ngày xưa đúng, nay không còn nữa. Dùng cho mọi chủ ngữ; sau “used to” là động từ nguyên mẫu.\nI [[used to]] walk to school every day.\nThere [[used to]] be a movie theater here.\nShe [[used to]] have really long hair.\n\ndidn't use to / Did… use to…?\nCâu phủ định và câu hỏi đã có “did”, nên “used” bỏ -d thành “use”: didn't use to, Did you use to…?\nHe [[didn't use to]] like coffee.\n[[Did]] you [[use to]] live near here? – Yes, I [[did]].\nWhat games [[did]] you [[use to]] play?\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: This is it! I used to live in that yellow house.\nB: So cute! Did you use to ________ as a kid?\nA: All the time. We used to play soccer until dark.\nB: Not me. I didn't use to ________ much. I was such a bookworm.\nA: Why am I not surprised? Hey, see that phone shop?\nB: What did it use to be?\nA: A noodle stall. My grandma used to take me there every Sunday.\nB: That's so sweet. My grandpa used to ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. Did you use to __play here__ as a kid?\na. walk to school\nb. ride a bike here\nc. fly kites here\n\n2. I didn't use to __go outside__ much.\na. play sports\nb. watch TV\nc. talk\n\n3. My grandpa used to __make me pancakes__.\na. take me fishing\nb. read me stories\nc. walk me to school\n",
