     "md": "Level 6/unit 4/unit 4.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 4 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nDennis and Erin are chatting on their lunch break.\nDennis: I bought a lottery ticket today. What **would** you **do if** you **won**?\nErin: Easy. **If** I **won**, **I'd quit** my job on the spot!\nDennis: Really? And then what? **You'd get** bored in a week.\nErin: No way. **I'd travel** the world and **buy** a beach house.\nDennis: Nice. **If** I **were** rich, **I'd open** a little coffee shop.\nErin: A coffee shop? **You'd** still **have to** work!\nDennis: Sure, but **I'd be** my own boss. **Would** you **come** by?\nErin: Only **if** I **got** free coffee!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. What would you do if you won?\nchange: “would‿you” (d + y → j)\nstrong: “What”, “do”, “won”\n“would you” nối thành “wu-jơ”. “won” đọc /wʌn/, giống hệt “one”. Câu hỏi Wh- xuống giọng ở cuối.\n\n2. If I won, I'd quit my job on the spot!\nlinking: “If‿I”, “job‿on”\nchange: “quit my” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “quit”, “spot”\n“If I” nối thành “i-fai”, “job on” thành “ja-ban”. Âm /t/ của “quit” không bật ra trước “my”. Âm /d/ của “I'd” rất nhẹ nhưng vẫn phải có.\n\n3. You'd still have to work!\nchange: “have to” (v → f)\nweak: “You'd”\nstrong: “still”, “work”\n“have to” (phải) đọc /ˈhæftə/ “hép-tơ”: âm /v/ biến thành /f/. “You'd” đọc nhanh /jʊd/; âm /d/ rất nhẹ trước “still” nhưng vẫn phải có.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nI'd, you'd, she'd (= would) đọc nhanh; âm /d/ rất nhẹ nhưng đừng bỏ, vì “I quit” là thì khác.\n“would you” nối thành “wu-jơ”, giống “did you” → “đi-jơ”.\n“have to” đọc /ˈhæftə/ “hép-tơ”, “has to” đọc /ˈhæstə/ “hés-tơ”.\nNhấn vào động từ chính ở cả hai vế: if I WON, I'd QUIT.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I'd quit my job on the spot!**\nMình sẽ nghỉ việc ngay lập tức!\n“on the spot” = ngay lập tức, tại chỗ, không cần suy nghĩ thêm.\nCách nói tương đương: I'd quit right away!\n\n**I'd be my own boss.**\nMình sẽ được tự làm chủ.\n“be your own boss” = tự kinh doanh, không phải làm thuê cho ai.\nCách nói tương đương: I'd work for myself.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nCâu điều kiện loại 2: If + quá khứ đơn, would + V\nNói về tình huống không có thật hoặc khó xảy ra. Vế “if” dùng quá khứ nhưng nói về hiện tại, tương lai; “would” thường rút gọn: I'd, you'd.\n[[If]] I [[had]] a car, [[I'd drive]] to work.\nShe [[would be]] happier [[if]] she [[lived]] by the sea.\n[[What would]] you [[do if]] you [[lost]] your phone?\n\nIf I were… / If I were you…\nVới “be”, dùng “were” cho mọi chủ ngữ; văn nói thân mật cũng hay dùng “was”. “If I were you, I'd…” là cách khuyên rất phổ biến.\n[[If]] it [[were]] Saturday, I'd sleep all day.\n[[If I were you]], I'd take the job.\n[[If]] he [[was]] here, he'd know what to do.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: I bought a lottery ticket today. What would you do if you won?\nB: Easy. If I won, I'd ________ on the spot!\nA: Really? And then what? You'd get bored in a week.\nB: No way. I'd travel the world and ________.\nA: Nice. If I were rich, I'd open a little coffee shop.\nB: A coffee shop? You'd still have to work!\nA: Sure, but I'd be my own boss. Would you come by?\nB: Only if I ________!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. If I won, I'd __quit my job__ on the spot!\na. buy a new car\nb. pay off my student loans\nc. book a flight to Paris\n\n2. I'd travel the world and __buy a beach house__.\na. learn to surf\nb. never cook again\nc. buy my parents a house\n\n3. Only if I __got free coffee__!\na. got a discount\nb. could sit by the window\nc. didn't have to pay\n",
