     "md": "Level 6/unit 5/unit 5.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 5 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nChloe and Patrick are about to leave for the airport. Chloe is checking everything one last time.\nChloe: Passports, tickets, chargers. Did you **remember to pack** the sunscreen?\nPatrick: Yep. I **remember putting** it in the blue bag.\nChloe: Great. And don't **forget to lock** the back door this time!\nPatrick: That was one time! I'm **trying to turn** the key, but it's stuck.\nChloe: **Try pulling** the door toward you while you turn it.\nPatrick: That worked! Can we **stop to get** coffee on the way?\nChloe: Sure. Wait, did I turn off the stove?\nPatrick: Yes, I watched you. Now **stop worrying** and let's hit the road!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. And don't forget to lock the back door this time!\nchange: “don't forget” (mất âm t)\nweak: “to”\nstrong: “lock”, “this time”\nÂm /t/ của “don't” mất trước “forget”: “đôn-fơ-ghét”. “forget to” chỉ đọc một âm /t/: “fơ-ghé-tơ”. Nhấn “this time” với giọng trêu.\n\n2. I'm trying to turn the key, but it's stuck.\nweak: “to”\nchange: “but‿it's” (t → d nhẹ)\nstrong: “key”, “stuck”\n“trying to” đọc nhanh: “trai-ing-tơ”. “but it's” nối thành “bơ-đits”: âm /t/ giữa hai nguyên âm đọc thành “d” nhẹ. Nhấn “stuck” để than phiền.\n\n3. Now stop worrying and let's hit the road!\nlinking: “worrying‿and”\nchange: “and let's” (mất âm d)\nstrong: “stop worrying”, “road”\n“worrying” đọc /ˈwɝːiɪŋ/ “wơ-ri-ing”, không phải “wo-ri”. “and let's” đọc “ơn-lets”. Âm /t/ của “hit” không bật ra trước “the”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nÂm /t/, /d/ cuối từ thường mất trước phụ âm: don't forget → “đôn-fơ-ghét”.\nHai âm /t/ đứng liền nhau chỉ đọc một lần: forget to → “fơ-ghé-tơ”.\n“to” sau remember, forget, try thường đọc nhẹ /tə/; nhấn vào động từ phía sau: forget to LOCK.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**That was one time!**\nCó mỗi một lần thôi mà!\nCâu tự bào chữa nửa đùa nửa thật khi bị nhắc lại một lỗi cũ.\nCách nói tương đương: It only happened once!\n\n**Let's hit the road!**\nMình lên đường thôi!\n“hit the road” là cách nói thân mật của “xuất phát, bắt đầu chuyến đi”.\nCách nói tương đương: Let's get going!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nremember / forget + to V hay V-ing?\nremember / forget + to V: nhớ / quên làm một việc (việc chưa làm). remember + V-ing: nhớ là mình đã làm việc gì (việc đã xảy ra).\n[[Remember to call]] Grandma tonight.\nI [[forgot to buy]] milk again.\nI [[remember meeting]] her at a party.\n\nstop / try + to V hay V-ing?\nstop + V-ing: ngừng làm; stop + to V: dừng lại để làm việc khác. try + to V: cố gắng làm; try + V-ing: thử làm xem có hiệu quả không.\nHe [[stopped smoking]] last year.\nWe [[stopped to take]] some photos.\nCan't sleep? [[Try drinking]] warm milk.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: Passports, tickets, chargers. Did you remember to pack the sunscreen?\nB: Yep. I remember putting it in the blue bag.\nA: Great. And don't forget to lock the back door this time!\nB: That was one time! I'm trying to ________, but it's stuck.\nA: Try pulling the door toward you while you turn it.\nB: That worked! Can we stop to ________ on the way?\nA: Sure. Wait, did I turn off the stove?\nB: Yes, I watched you. Now stop ________ and let's hit the road!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. I'm trying to __turn the key__, but it's stuck.\na. close the window\nb. zip up my suitcase\nc. open the garage door\n\n2. Can we stop to __get coffee__ on the way?\na. grab breakfast\nb. buy snacks\nc. get some cash\n\n3. Now stop __worrying__ and let's hit the road!\na. checking everything\nb. panicking\nc. thinking about the stove\n",
