     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 6 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nVictor and Vivian are at a wedding reception. Victor doesn't know many of the guests.\nVictor: Do you know the guy **who's** giving the speech? He's hilarious.\nVivian: That's Marco, the groom's brother. He's the one **who** introduced them.\nVictor: Oh, that's sweet. And the woman in the green dress?\nVivian: She owns the café **where** they had their first date.\nVictor: Cute! Is she the one **who** made this amazing cake?\nVivian: No, the cake is from a bakery **that** my aunt runs.\nVictor: Your family's everywhere! And the man **who's** dancing on the table?\nVivian: Oh no, that's my dad. Pretend you didn't see that!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. He's the one who introduced them.\nlinking: “who‿introduced”\nchange: “introduced them” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “one”, “introduced”\n“who introduced” nối liền nhờ âm /w/ chen vào: “hu-win-trơ-đust”. Đuôi -ed đọc /t/ nhưng gần như mất trước “them”: “in-trơ-đus-đơm”.\n\n2. She owns the café where they had their first date.\nchange: “first date” (mất âm t)\nweak: “the”, “their”\nstrong: “owns”, “café”\nÂm /t/ của “first” mất vì kẹp giữa /s/ và /d/: “fơs-đêit”. “café” nhấn âm cuối: /kæˈfeɪ/ “ke-FÊI”.\n\n3. Pretend you didn't see that!\nchange: “Pretend‿you”, “didn't see”\nstrong: “Pretend”, “didn't see”\n“Pretend you” nối thành “pri-ten-jơ” (d + y → j), giống “did you” → “đi-jơ”. Âm /t/ của “didn't” gần như mất trước “see”: “đi-đần-si”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“who, that, where” trong mệnh đề quan hệ đọc nhẹ và nối liền với từ đứng trước.\n“that” làm đại từ quan hệ đọc nhẹ /ðət/; “that” chỉ trỏ (that guy) mới đọc mạnh /ðæt/.\nKhông ngắt giọng trước mệnh đề quan hệ: “a bakery that my aunt runs” đọc như một cụm.\n“who's” (= who is) đọc /huːz/, giống hệt “whose”: the guy who's giving the speech.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**He's hilarious.**\nAnh ấy hài hước cực kỳ.\n“hilarious” /hɪˈleriəs/ mạnh hơn “funny” nhiều: buồn cười đến mức cười mãi không thôi.\nCách nói tương đương: He's so funny.\n\n**Pretend you didn't see that!**\nCoi như bạn chưa thấy gì nhé!\nCâu nói đùa khi người thân của mình làm điều gì đó xấu hổ trước mặt người khác.\nCách nói tương đương: You didn't see anything, OK?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nMệnh đề quan hệ: who / which / that\nĐứng ngay sau danh từ để nói rõ người, vật nào. Người: who / that; vật: which / that. Không có dấu phẩy. Người Mỹ dùng “that” nhiều hơn “which”.\nThe man [[who]] lives next door is a pilot.\nWhere's the charger [[that]] was on my desk?\nI want a phone [[which]] has a good camera.\n\nwhere và lược bỏ that\nwhere + mệnh đề (chủ ngữ + động từ) dùng cho nơi chốn. Khi who / that / which là tân ngữ, có thể bỏ: the cake (that) she made.\nThis is the hospital [[where]] I was born.\nIs there a shop [[where]] I can buy stamps?\nThe dress ([[that]]) she's wearing is gorgeous.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Do you know the guy who's giving the speech? He's hilarious.\nB: That's Marco, the groom's brother. He's the one who ________.\nA: Oh, that's sweet. And the woman in the green dress?\nB: She owns the café where ________.\nA: Cute! Is she the one who made this amazing cake?\nB: No, the cake is from a bakery ________.\nA: Your family's everywhere! And the man who's dancing on the table?\nB: Oh no, that's my dad. Pretend you didn't see that!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. He's the one who __introduced them__.\na. planned the wedding\nb. sang at the ceremony\nc. booked the band\n\n2. She owns the café where __they had their first date__.\na. they first met\nb. they got engaged\nc. the groom works\n\n3. No, the cake is from a bakery __that my aunt runs__.\na. that my cousin owns\nb. that opened last month\nc. that's near my office\n",
