     "md": "Level 6/unit 7/unit 7.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 7 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nIvan is a tour guide. He's showing Paula around an old opera house.\nPaula: Wow, this building is gorgeous! When **was** it **built**?\nIvan: It **was built** over a hundred years ago, by a French architect.\nPaula: And these paintings on the ceiling? They're incredible.\nIvan: They **were painted** by six local artists. It took them four years!\nPaula: Amazing. **Is** it still **used** today?\nIvan: Yes, operas **are performed** here every weekend.\nPaula: I'd love to see one. **Are** photos **allowed** in here?\nIvan: Sure, but no flash, please. The old paint **is** easily **damaged**.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. When was it built?\nlinking: “was‿it”\nweak: “was”\nstrong: “When”, “built”\n“was it” nối thành “wơ-zit”. “built” đọc /bɪlt/ “bilt”, chữ “u” câm. Câu hỏi Wh- xuống giọng ở cuối.\n\n2. They were painted by six local artists.\nweak: “were”, “by”\nchange: “painted” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “six”, “local artists”\n“were” đọc nhẹ /wər/ “wơ”. Giọng Mỹ hay bỏ âm /t/ đứng sau /n/: painted → “pây-nịd”. “local artists” nối thành “lâu-cơ-lar-đists”.\n\n3. Yes, operas are performed here every weekend.\nlinking: “operas‿are”\nweak: “are”\nstrong: “performed”, “every weekend”\n“operas are” nối thành “a-pơ-rơ-zơ”, “are” đọc nhẹ /ər/. Đuôi -ed của “performed” đọc /d/: “pơ-formd”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nTrong câu bị động, “is / are / was / were” đọc nhẹ; nhấn vào V3: it was BUILT.\nGiọng Mỹ hay bỏ /t/ sau /n/: painted → “pây-nịd”, twenty → “twe-ni”.\nĐuôi -ed đọc /d/ sau âm hữu thanh (performed, used), đọc /ɪd/ sau t, d (painted).\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**It took them four years!**\nHọ mất bốn năm mới vẽ xong đấy!\n“It takes / took + người + thời gian” = ai đó mất bao lâu để làm việc gì.\nCách nói tương đương: They spent four years on it!\n\n**No flash, please.**\nVui lòng không dùng đèn flash.\nLời nhắc ngắn, lịch sự hay gặp ở bảo tàng, nhà hát. “flash” là đèn chớp của máy ảnh.\nCách nói tương đương: Please don't use your flash.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nBị động: be + V3\nDùng khi hành động hoặc vật chịu tác động quan trọng hơn người làm. Hiện tại: am / is / are + V3; quá khứ: was / were + V3.\nEnglish [[is spoken]] all over the world.\nThis bridge [[was built]] by the French.\nThe windows [[are cleaned]] every Monday.\n\nCâu hỏi, phủ định và by + người làm\nHỏi: đảo “be” lên trước (Was it built…?). Phủ định: isn't / wasn't + V3. Chỉ thêm “by + người làm” khi thông tin đó thật sự quan trọng.\n[[Was]] the room [[cleaned]] this morning?\nSmoking [[isn't allowed]] inside.\nThis song [[was written by]] a ten-year-old girl.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Wow, this building is gorgeous! When was it built?\nB: It ________ over a hundred years ago, by a French architect.\nA: And these paintings on the ceiling? They're incredible.\nB: They were painted by ________. It took them four years!\nA: Amazing. Is it still used today?\nB: Yes, ________ here every weekend.\nA: I'd love to see one. Are photos allowed in here?\nB: Sure, but no flash, please. The old paint is easily damaged.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. It __was built__ over a hundred years ago, by a French architect.\na. was designed\nb. was completed\nc. was rebuilt\n\n2. They were painted by __six local artists__.\na. an Italian painter\nb. a team of students\nc. the architect's wife\n\n3. Yes, __operas are performed__ here every weekend.\na. concerts are held\nb. weddings are held\nc. tours are given\n",
