     "folder": "Level 6/unit 8",
     "md": "Level 6/unit 8/unit 8.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 8 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nToan is back from lunch. His coworker Huong has a message from their boss, Diane.\nToan: Hey, Huong. Did Diane call while I was at lunch?\nHuong: Yes. She **said** her flight **was** delayed.\nToan: Oh no. What about our meeting at three?\nHuong: She **told** me she **couldn't** make it. She **said** we **could** start without her.\nToan: OK. Did she say anything about my report?\nHuong: She **said** it **was** really good, but it **needed** more charts.\nToan: More charts? She **told** me it **was** perfect yesterday!\nHuong: Don't worry. She **said** **she'd** call you tonight.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. She said her flight was delayed.\nlinking: “said‿her” (mất âm h)\nweak: “her”, “was”\nstrong: “flight”, “delayed”\n“her” đọc nhẹ nên mất âm /h/, nối với “said” thành “se-đơ”. “was” đọc nhẹ /wəz/. Nhấn vào tin chính: “flight”, “delayed”.\n\n2. She told me she couldn't make it.\nchange: “told me”, “couldn't make”\nlinking: “make‿it”\nstrong: “couldn't”\nÂm /d/ của “told” và /t/ của “couldn't” gần như mất trước phụ âm: “tôl-mi”, “cu-đần-mêi-kit”. Nhấn “couldn't” vì đó là tin chính.\n\n3. She said she'd call you tonight.\nweak: “she'd”\nlinking: “call‿you”\nstrong: “call”, “tonight”\n“she'd” (= she would) đọc /ʃiːd/; âm /d/ rất nhẹ trước “call” nhưng không được bỏ. “call you” nối thành “co-lyơ”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCâu tường thuật có nhiều từ nhẹ (she, her, was); nhấn vào thông tin mới: her FLIGHT was DELAYED.\n“her, him, his” đọc nhẹ thường mất âm /h/: said her → “se-đơ”.\nshe'd, he'd, they'd (= would) đọc nhanh, âm /d/ rất nhẹ.\n“said” đọc /sed/, vần với “bed”; đừng đọc /seɪd/ như “say” thêm âm d.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**She couldn't make it.**\nChị ấy không đến được.\n“make it” = đến được, tham dự được (cuộc họp, bữa tiệc…) hoặc đến kịp giờ.\nCách nói tương đương: She couldn't come.\n\n**Did she say anything about my report?**\nChị ấy có nói gì về bản báo cáo của tôi không?\n“say anything about…” dùng để hỏi xem ai đó có nhắc đến chuyện gì không.\nCách nói tương đương: Did she mention my report?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nCâu tường thuật: lùi thì\nKhi kể lại lời người khác bằng said / told, động từ thường lùi một thì: am / is → was, can → could, will → would, need → needed.\nShe [[said]] she [[was]] hungry.\nTom [[told]] me he [[could]] fix it.\nThey [[said]] they [[would]] call back.\n\nsaid hay told?\nsaid (that) + mệnh đề, không cần người nghe. told + người nghe + (that) + mệnh đề. Không nói “said me”. Khi nói, “that” thường được bỏ.\nHe [[said]] (that) he was busy.\nShe [[told me]] she was leaving.\nMy boss [[told us]] the office was closing early.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: Hey, Huong. Did Diane call while I was at lunch?\nB: Yes. She said her flight ________.\nA: Oh no. What about our meeting at three?\nB: She told me she ________. She said we could start without her.\nA: OK. Did she say anything about my report?\nB: She said it was really good, but it ________.\nA: More charts? She told me it was perfect yesterday!\nB: Don't worry. She said she'd call you tonight.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. She said her flight __was delayed__.\na. was canceled\nb. was two hours late\nc. was overbooked\n\n2. She told me she __couldn't make it__.\na. wouldn't be back today\nb. was too busy\nc. had another meeting\n\n3. She said it was really good, but it __needed more charts__.\na. was a little long\nb. had a few typos\nc. needed more examples\n",
