     "md": "Level 7/unit 1/unit 1.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 1 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nAaron is moving out tomorrow. His friend Bella comes over to help him pack.\nBella: Wow, you look exhausted! What **have** you **been doing**?\nAaron: **I've been packing** since six. My back is killing me.\nBella: Yikes. So how many boxes have you done?\nAaron: Only twelve, believe it or not. **I've been going through** old stuff all day.\nBella: Oh, that's always the slowest part. Find anything good?\nAaron: Tons of old photos. **I've been laughing** at my high school haircut for an hour.\nBella: Ha! I need to see that. But first, where's the tape?\nAaron: Under that pile of shirts, I think. Thanks for coming, seriously.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. What have you been doing?\nchange: “What have” (t → d nhẹ)\nweak: “have”, “you”, “been”\nstrong: “doing”\n“What have” nối thành “wa-đơv”: âm /h/ của “have” mất, /t/ đọc như “d” nhẹ. Cả câu nghe như “wa-đơv-yơ-bin-đu-ing”, nhấn vào “doing”.\n\n2. I've been going through old stuff all day.\nchange: “old stuff” (mất âm d)\nlinking: “stuff‿all‿day”\nstrong: “going through”, “all day”\nÂm /d/ của “old” kẹp giữa hai phụ âm nên bị nuốt: “ôl-stớf”. “stuff all day” nối liền: “stớ-fol-đây”. “I've been” lướt nhanh, nhẹ: “aiv-bin”.\n\n3. I've been laughing at my high school haircut for an hour.\nlinking: “laughing‿at”, “for‿an‿hour”\nstrong: “high”, “haircut”\n“laughing at” nối thành “le-phin-gơt”. Danh từ ghép nhấn âm đầu: HIGH school, HAIRcut. “for an hour” nối liền, chữ “h” câm: “fơ-rơ-nao-ơr”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“been” trong giọng Mỹ đọc ngắn, nhẹ /bɪn/ “bin”, không kéo dài thành “biin”.\n“have” sau từ để hỏi đọc nhẹ /əv/: What have you → “wa-đơv-yơ”.\nÂm /d/, /t/ cuối từ hay bị nuốt trước phụ âm: old stuff → “ôl-stớf”, need to → “ni-tơ”.\nNhấn vào hoạt động và thời gian: I've been PACKING since SIX.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**My back is killing me.**\nLưng mình đau chết đi được.\n“… is killing me” là cách nói phóng đại khi một chỗ trên cơ thể rất đau: My feet are killing me.\nCách nói tương đương: My back really hurts.\n\n**Only twelve, believe it or not.**\nMới có mười hai thùng, nói ra chắc bạn không tin.\n“believe it or not” chèn vào khi kể điều đáng ngạc nhiên, đặt đầu hoặc cuối câu đều được.\nCách nói tương đương: Would you believe it? Only twelve.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nHiện tại hoàn thành tiếp diễn: have / has been + V-ing\nViệc bắt đầu trong quá khứ, kéo dài đến bây giờ hoặc vừa dừng và còn để lại dấu vết. Hay đi với for, since, all day, How long…?\n[[She's been learning]] Korean for two years.\nThe street is wet. [[It's been raining]].\nHow long [[have]] you [[been waiting]]? – Not long.\n\nhave been + V-ing hay have + V3?\nNhấn vào quá trình, khoảng thời gian → have been + V-ing. Nhấn vào kết quả, số lượng đã làm xong → have + V3.\n[[I've been writing]] emails all morning.\n[[I've written]] fifteen emails so far.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: Wow, you look exhausted! What have you been doing?\nB: I've been ________ since six. My back is killing me.\nA: Yikes. So how many boxes have you done?\nB: Only twelve, believe it or not. I've been going through old stuff all day.\nA: Oh, that's always the slowest part. Find anything good?\nB: Tons of old photos. I've been laughing at my high school haircut ________.\nA: Ha! I need to see that. But first, where's the tape?\nB: Under that pile of shirts, I think. Thanks for ________, seriously.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. I've been __packing__ since six.\na. cleaning the kitchen\nb. carrying boxes\nc. wrapping dishes\n\n2. I've been laughing at my high school haircut __for an hour__.\na. since lunch\nb. all afternoon\nc. for twenty minutes\n\n3. Thanks for __coming__, seriously.\na. helping out\nb. bringing lunch\nc. giving up your Saturday\n",
