     "md": "Level 7/unit 2/unit 2.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 2 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nJade got to work two hours late today. At lunch, her coworker Colin asks what happened.\nColin: So what happened this morning? You're never late.\nJade: Total nightmare. By the time I got to the station, my train **had already left**.\nColin: Oh no. Did you wait for the next one?\nJade: I was about to, but then I realized **I'd left** my wallet at home.\nColin: Oh, that's the worst! So you went all the way back?\nJade: Yep. And then the next train got stuck in a tunnel for forty minutes.\nColin: What a morning! You should've just stayed in bed.\nJade: No kidding. I just noticed **I'd put on** two different shoes.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. By the time I got to the station, my train had already left.\nsmooth: “By the time I”\nweak: “had”\nstrong: “already left”\n“By the time I” đọc liền một hơi: “bai-đơ-tai-mai”. “had” đọc nhẹ /həd/, nối vào “already”: “hơ-đol-re-đi”. Nhấn “already left”: tàu đi mất trước khi mình tới.\n\n2. And then the next train got stuck in a tunnel for forty minutes.\nchange: “next train” (mất âm t)\nlinking: “stuck‿in‿a”\nstrong: “forty minutes”\nÂm /t/ của “next” kẹp giữa hai phụ âm nên bị nuốt: “nex-trein”. “stuck in a” nối thành “stơ-ki-nơ”. Giọng Mỹ đọc “forty” thành “for-đi”.\n\n3. I just noticed I'd put on two different shoes.\nchange: “just noticed” (mất âm t)\nlinking: “put‿on”\nstrong: “two different shoes”\n“just noticed” đọc /dʒʌs ˈnoʊtɪst/, âm /t/ của “just” mất. “put on” nối thành “pu-đon”. “I'd” = I had: xỏ nhầm giày từ trước lúc phát hiện.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“had” trong quá khứ hoàn thành đọc nhẹ /həd/, hay rút gọn thành 'd: I'd, she'd, they'd.\n“I'd” + V3 (left, gone) = I had; “I'd” + động từ nguyên mẫu = I would.\nÂm /t/ kẹp giữa hai phụ âm thường bị nuốt: next train → “nex-trein”.\nKhi kể chuyện xui, nhấn vào chi tiết bất ngờ nhất: TWO DIFFERENT SHOES.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Total nightmare.**\nĐúng là ác mộng.\nDạng rút gọn của “It was a total nightmare”, dùng để than về một trải nghiệm tồi tệ.\nCách nói tương đương: It was a disaster.\n\n**I was about to, but then…**\nMình vừa định thế thì…\n“be about to + V” = sắp sửa làm gì. Nói “I was about to” rồi dừng, ngụ ý việc đó không thành.\nCách nói tương đương: I was going to, but…\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nQuá khứ hoàn thành: had + V3\nDùng cho việc xảy ra TRƯỚC một việc khác trong quá khứ; việc xảy ra sau dùng quá khứ đơn. Khi nói, “had” thường rút gọn thành 'd.\nWhen we arrived, the movie [[had]] already [[started]].\nShe [[hadn't eaten]] all day, so she was starving.\n[[I'd]] never [[seen]] snow before that trip.\n\nBy the time / realized / found out + quá khứ hoàn thành\nSau “By the time + quá khứ đơn”, vế chính dùng had + V3. Sau realized, noticed, found out…, việc xảy ra trước đó dùng had + V3.\n[[By the time]] he called, [[I'd gone]] to bed.\nShe [[realized]] she [[had lost]] her keys.\nWe [[found out]] the store [[had closed]].\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: So what happened this morning? You're never late.\nB: Total nightmare. By the time I got to the station, my train ________.\nA: Oh no. Did you wait for the next one?\nB: I was about to, but then I realized ________.\nA: Oh, that's the worst! So you went all the way back?\nB: Yep. And then the next train got stuck in a tunnel for forty minutes.\nA: What a morning! You should've just stayed in bed.\nB: No kidding. I just noticed I'd put on ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. By the time I got to the station, my train __had already left__.\na. had just pulled out\nb. had been canceled\nc. had left without me\n\n2. I was about to, but then I realized __I'd left my wallet at home__.\na. I'd forgotten my phone\nb. I'd lost my train pass\nc. I'd brought the wrong bag\n\n3. I just noticed I'd put on __two different shoes__.\na. my sweater inside out\nb. two different earrings\nc. my shirt backwards\n",
