     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 3 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nTickets for Leah and Derek's favorite band went on sale this morning. Derek tried to buy two.\nLeah: So? Please tell me we're going!\nDerek: Bad news. I had two tickets in my cart, and then my card got declined.\nLeah: No way! What happened?\nDerek: My bank thought it was fraud. **If I'd used** my other card, we **would've been** fine.\nLeah: Couldn't you just switch to the other one?\nDerek: I tried, but they sold out in eight minutes!\nLeah: Oh well. **If we'd gone**, **we'd have been** stuck way in the back anyway.\nDerek: True. And I **wouldn't have heard** a thing over your singing.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. If I'd used my other card, we would've been fine.\nlinking: “If‿I'd”\nweak: “would've”\nstrong: “other card”, “fine”\n“If I'd” nối thành “i-faid”, âm /d/ rất nhẹ nhưng không bỏ. “would've” = would have, đọc nhẹ /ˈwʊdəv/, nối vào “been”: “wu-đơv-bin”.\n\n2. If we'd gone, we'd have been stuck way in the back anyway.\nweak: “we'd have been”\nstrong: “stuck”, “way in the back”\n“we'd” đầu là we had (theo sau là V3 “gone”); “we'd” sau là we would (theo sau là “have”). “we'd have been” lướt nhanh: “wi-đơv-bin”.\n\n3. And I wouldn't have heard a thing over your singing.\nchange: “wouldn't have” (→ /ˈwʊdntəv/)\nlinking: “heard‿a”\nstrong: “thing”, “singing”\n“wouldn't have” khi nói nhanh còn /ˈwʊdntəv/ “wu-đơn-tơv”. “heard a” nối thành “hơr-đơ”. Giọng trêu đùa, nhấn vào “singing”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nwould've / could've / should've: “have” đọc nhẹ /əv/ → “wu-đơv”, “cu-đơv”, “shu-đơv”. Đừng viết thành “would of”.\n'd + V3 = had (we'd gone); 'd + have hoặc động từ nguyên mẫu = would (we'd have been).\nÂm /t/ gặp /j/ (you) biến thành “ch”: Couldn't you → “cu-đơn-chu”.\nCâu tiếc nuối nhấn vào chi tiết “giá mà”: If I'd used my OTHER CARD…\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Please tell me we're going!**\nLàm ơn bảo là tụi mình được đi xem nhé!\n“Please tell me + mệnh đề” = mình rất mong điều đó là thật (và hơi lo là không phải).\nCách nói tương đương: We're going, right? Say yes!\n\n**My card got declined.**\nThẻ của mình bị từ chối thanh toán.\n“get + V3” mang nghĩa bị động, rất hay dùng trong văn nói: got declined, got canceled.\nCách nói tương đương: My card didn't go through.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nCâu điều kiện loại 3: If + had + V3, would have + V3\nTưởng tượng một quá khứ khác với sự thật, thường để tiếc nuối hoặc trách móc. Khi nói: If I'd…, I would've / I'd have…\n[[If]] she [[had studied]], she [[would have passed]].\n[[If I'd known]], [[I would've]] called you.\nWe [[wouldn't have]] gotten lost [[if]] you'd listened.\n\nPhủ định và cách nhận ra 'd\n'd + V3 = had; 'd + have = would. Phủ định: If… hadn't + V3, … wouldn't have + V3.\n[[If]] it [[hadn't rained]], [[we'd have]] gone hiking.\nShe [[wouldn't have]] come [[if]] you [[hadn't]] invited her.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: So? Please tell me we're going!\nB: Bad news. I had two tickets in my cart, and then ________.\nA: No way! What happened?\nB: My bank thought it was fraud. If I'd ________, we would've been fine.\nA: Couldn't you just switch to the other one?\nB: I tried, but they sold out in eight minutes!\nA: Oh well. If we'd gone, we'd have been stuck way in the back anyway.\nB: True. And I wouldn't have heard a thing over ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. I had two tickets in my cart, and then __my card got declined__.\na. the site crashed\nb. my phone died\nc. the Wi-Fi went down\n\n2. If I'd __used my other card__, we would've been fine.\na. paid with my phone\nb. called the bank first\nc. been a bit faster\n\n3. And I wouldn't have heard a thing over __your singing__.\na. the crowd\nb. all the screaming\nc. the guy next to us\n",
