     "md": "Level 7/unit 5/unit 5.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 5 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nFelix had a job interview this morning. His friend Tessa wants to hear all about it.\nTessa: So, how did it go? Tell me everything!\nFelix: Pretty well, I think. First, they **asked me to talk** about myself for two minutes.\nTessa: Only two minutes? That's tough. What else?\nFelix: Then the manager **asked if I'd** ever led a team, and **why I wanted** to leave.\nTessa: Classic. What did you tell her?\nFelix: The truth, mostly. Oh, and they **asked me to solve** a logic puzzle on the whiteboard.\nTessa: A puzzle? You're kidding! Did you crack it?\nFelix: Eventually. And at the end, they **asked when I could** start!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. First, they asked me to talk about myself for two minutes.\nchange: “asked me” (mất âm k, t)\nlinking: “talk‿about”\nstrong: “myself”, “two minutes”\n“asked” có cụm /skt/; trước phụ âm thường chỉ còn “és”: asked me → “és-mi”. “talk about” nối thành “to-kơ-baot”, chữ “l” trong “talk” câm.\n\n2. Then the manager asked if I'd ever led a team, and why I wanted to leave.\nlinking: “asked‿if‿I'd‿ever”\nchange: “wanted” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “led a team”, “leave”\n“asked if I'd ever” nối liền: “és-ti-fai-đe-vơr”; “I'd” ở đây là “I had”. Giọng Mỹ hay bỏ /t/ sau /n/: wanted → “wa-nịd”.\n\n3. What did you tell her?\nchange: “did you” (d + y → “j”)\nlinking: “tell‿her”\nstrong: “tell”\n“did you” đọc thành “đi-jơ”. “her” đọc nhẹ, mất âm /h/ và nối vào “tell”: “te-lơ”. Cả câu: “wa-đi-jơ-te-lơ”, xuống giọng ở cuối.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“asked” trước phụ âm thường chỉ còn “és”: asked me → “és-mi”.\nCâu hỏi tường thuật là câu kể: không đảo ngữ, xuống giọng ở cuối.\nGiọng Mỹ hay bỏ /t/ sau /n/: wanted → “wa-nịd”, interview → “i-nơ-viu”.\n“her, him, his” đọc nhẹ thường mất âm /h/: tell her → “te-lơ”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Classic.**\nCâu kinh điển luôn.\n“Classic.” (văn nói) = đúng kiểu quen thuộc, ai cũng đoán trước được; ở đây ý là câu hỏi phỏng vấn kinh điển.\nCách nói tương đương: Of course they asked that.\n\n**Did you crack it?**\nBạn có giải được không?\n“crack” (văn nói) = giải được một câu đố, mật mã hay vấn đề khó.\nCách nói tương đương: Did you figure it out?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nTường thuật câu hỏi: asked if / asked + từ để hỏi\nCâu hỏi Yes/No → asked (me) if…; câu hỏi Wh- → giữ từ để hỏi. Chủ ngữ đứng trước động từ, bỏ do / did và lùi thì.\nShe [[asked if]] I [[was]] free on Friday.\nThey [[asked where]] I [[lived]].\nHe [[asked how long]] [[I'd worked]] there.\n\nTường thuật lời yêu cầu: asked / told + người + to V\nLời nhờ (Can you…? / Please…) → asked + người + to V; phủ định: not to V. “told” mạnh hơn, giống mệnh lệnh.\nMy boss [[asked me to stay]] late.\nShe [[asked us not to]] park here.\nThe doctor [[told him to rest]] for a week.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: So, how did it go? Tell me everything!\nB: Pretty well, I think. First, they asked me ________ for two minutes.\nA: Only two minutes? That's tough. What else?\nB: Then the manager asked if I'd ever ________, and why I wanted to leave.\nA: Classic. What did you tell her?\nB: The truth, mostly. Oh, and they asked me to solve a logic puzzle on the whiteboard.\nA: A puzzle? You're kidding! Did you crack it?\nB: Eventually. And at the end, they asked ________!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. First, they asked me __to talk about myself__ for two minutes.\na. to describe my last project\nb. to pitch a new idea\nc. to introduce myself in English\n\n2. Then the manager asked if I'd ever __led a team__, and why I wanted to leave.\na. worked abroad\nb. managed a budget\nc. dealt with angry customers\n\n3. And at the end, they asked __when I could start__!\na. if I could start next week\nb. what salary I'd expect\nc. if I had any other offers\n",
