     "md": "Level 7/unit 6/unit 6.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 6 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nGordon and Carmen are going over the checklist for their company's anniversary party.\nGordon: Final check for Friday. **Have** the invitations **been sent** out?\nCarmen: Yep, last week. And the hall **has been booked** for the whole evening.\nGordon: Great. And the food? Last year it showed up an hour late.\nCarmen: I remember. This time, it **must be delivered** by five, or we don't pay.\nGordon: Smart. And who's setting up the tables?\nCarmen: The venue staff. Apparently, it **can all be done** in an hour.\nGordon: One more thing. **Has** the projector **been tested**? I don't want another disaster.\nCarmen: Twice. Relax, Gordon. **Everything's been taken care of**.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. And the hall has been booked for the whole evening.\nlinking: “hall‿has‿been”\nstrong: “booked”, “whole evening”\n“has” đọc nhẹ /əz/, mất âm /h/, nối vào “hall”: “ho-lơz-bin”. Nhấn “booked”: việc đã xong.\n\n2. Last year it showed up an hour late.\nchange: “Last year” (t + y → “ch”)\nlinking: “showed‿up‿an‿hour”\nstrong: “late”\n“Last year” thường đọc thành “las-chiơr”. “showed up an hour” nối thành một chuỗi: “shâu-đớ-pơ-nao-ơr”; chữ “h” trong “hour” câm. Nhấn “late” để than phiền.\n\n3. This time, it must be delivered by five, or we don't pay.\nchange: “must be”, “don't pay” (mất âm t; n → m)\nstrong: “delivered”, “five”\n“must be” mất âm /t/: “mớs-bi”. “don't pay” mất /t/, rồi /n/ biến thành /m/ trước /p/: “đôm-pây”. Nhấn vào thời hạn.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nBị động hoàn thành: “has / have been” đọc nhẹ, lướt nhanh: has been → “ơz-bin”, it's been → “its-bin”.\nBị động với modal: modal và “be” đọc nhẹ, nhấn vào V3: it must be DELIVERED.\nÂm /t/ kẹp giữa hai phụ âm thường mất: must be → “mớs-bi”, booked for → “búk-fơr”.\nÂm /n/ trước /p/, /b/, /m/ dễ biến thành /m/: don't pay → “đôm-pây”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Last year it showed up an hour late.**\nNăm ngoái đồ ăn tới trễ cả tiếng.\n“show up” (văn nói) = đến, xuất hiện; hay dùng khi ai hoặc cái gì đến trễ, hoặc không đến.\nCách nói tương đương: It arrived an hour late.\n\n**Everything's been taken care of.**\nMọi thứ đã được lo xong hết rồi.\n“take care of” = lo liệu, xử lý; dạng bị động “be taken care of” hay dùng để trấn an người khác.\nCách nói tương đương: It's all been handled.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nBị động với modal: can / must / should / will + be + V3\nDùng khi việc cần làm quan trọng hơn người làm. Phủ định: can't / shouldn't / won't + be + V3.\nThe form [[must be signed]] by Friday.\nThis door [[can't be opened]] from outside.\nThe results [[will be announced]] tomorrow.\n\nBị động hiện tại hoàn thành: has / have been + V3\nNói việc đã được làm xong (hoặc chưa), không cần biết ai làm. Hay đi với already, yet, just; khi nói thường rút gọn: it's been, they've been.\nYour order [[has been shipped]].\n[[Has]] the room [[been cleaned]] yet? – Not yet.\nAll the tickets [[have]] already [[been sold]].\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Final check for Friday. Have the invitations been sent out?\nB: Yep, last week. And ________ has been booked for the whole evening.\nA: Great. And the food? Last year it showed up an hour late.\nB: I remember. This time, it ________ by five, or we don't pay.\nA: Smart. And who's setting up the tables?\nB: The venue staff. Apparently, it can all be done in an hour.\nA: One more thing. Has the projector been tested? I don't want another disaster.\nB: Twice. Relax, Gordon. Everything's been ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. And __the hall__ has been booked for the whole evening.\na. the band\nb. a photographer\nc. the rooftop bar\n\n2. This time, it __must be delivered__ by five, or we don't pay.\na. has to be delivered\nb. needs to be here\nc. must be set up\n\n3. Relax, Gordon. Everything's been __taken care of__.\na. paid for\nb. double-checked\nc. sorted out\n",
