     "md": "Level 7/unit 7/unit 7.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 7 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nGiang is showing her friend Ian around her hometown, Hue.\nIan: Wow, these walls are huge! How old is this place?\nGiang: It's the Imperial City, **which** was built over two hundred years ago.\nIan: Amazing. And the emperors actually lived here?\nGiang: Yes. That hall over there, **where** they were crowned, is my favorite part.\nIan: Beautiful. So, where to next?\nGiang: Dong Ba Market. My aunt, **whose** stall sells conical hats, will give you a good price.\nIan: Perfect! Can we grab a bite there too? I'm starving.\nGiang: Sure. Let's get bun bo, **which** is way spicier than pho. Hope you can handle the heat!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. It's the Imperial City, which was built over two hundred years ago.\nlinking: “years‿ago”\nweak: “was”\nstrong: “Imperial City”, “two hundred”\nNgắt nhẹ ở dấu phẩy trước “which”: phần sau chỉ là thông tin thêm. “was” đọc nhẹ /wəz/; “years ago” nối thành “yiơr-zơ-gâu”.\n\n2. That hall over there, where they were crowned, is my favorite part.\nweak: “they were”\nstrong: “hall”, “favorite part”\nPhần giữa hai dấu phẩy đọc nhanh và thấp giọng hơn, như lời chú thích. “favorite” thường đọc gọn hai âm tiết: “fây-vrịt”.\n\n3. My aunt, whose stall sells conical hats, will give you a good price.\nchange: “good price” (d → b)\nstrong: “aunt”, “conical hats”\nGiọng Mỹ đọc “aunt” giống “ant” /ænt/; “whose” đọc giống “who's”. Âm /d/ của “good” biến thành /b/ trước /p/: “gúb-prais”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nMệnh đề có dấu phẩy: ngắt nhẹ trước và sau, đọc phần chú thích thấp giọng hơn.\n“which” đọc giống “witch”; “whose” đọc giống “who's” /huːz/.\nÂm /d/, /t/, /n/ cuối từ dễ biến thành /b/, /p/, /m/ khi đứng trước /b/, /p/, /m/: good price → “gúb-prais”.\nKhi giới thiệu địa danh, nhấn vào tên riêng và con số: the IMPERIAL CITY, TWO HUNDRED years.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**So, where to next?**\nTiếp theo mình đi đâu đây?\nCâu hỏi rút gọn của “Where are we going next?”, rất hay dùng khi đi chơi, tham quan.\nCách nói tương đương: What's next?\n\n**Hope you can handle the heat!**\nMong là bạn ăn cay được nhé!\nVăn nói hay bỏ chủ ngữ “I” trước “hope”. “the heat” ở đây là độ cay của ớt, không phải trời nóng.\nCách nói tương đương: I hope you like spicy food!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nMệnh đề quan hệ không xác định: dấu phẩy + which / who\nThêm thông tin phụ về người hoặc vật đã rõ là ai, cái gì. Luôn có dấu phẩy, bỏ đi câu vẫn đủ nghĩa; không dùng “that” thay cho which / who.\nMy brother, [[who]] lives in Da Lat, is a chef.\nHa Long Bay, [[which]] I visited last year, is stunning.\n\nwhose / where trong mệnh đề quan hệ\n“whose + danh từ” = của người hoặc vật đó; “where” = ở nơi đó (thay cho in which / at which).\nMy neighbor, [[whose]] dog barks all night, is moving.\nWe stayed in Hoi An, [[where]] my parents first met.\nThat's the café [[where]] I work.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Wow, these walls are huge! How old is this place?\nB: It's the Imperial City, which was built ________.\nA: Amazing. And the emperors actually lived here?\nB: Yes. That hall over there, where they were crowned, is my favorite part.\nA: Beautiful. So, where to next?\nB: Dong Ba Market. My aunt, ________, will give you a good price.\nA: Perfect! Can we grab a bite there too? I'm starving.\nB: Sure. Let's get bun bo, which is ________. Hope you can handle the heat!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. It's the Imperial City, which was built __over two hundred years ago__.\na. in the early eighteen hundreds\nb. by the Nguyen emperors\nc. for the royal family\n\n2. My aunt, __whose stall sells conical hats__, will give you a good price.\na. whose shop is near the entrance\nb. who sells silk scarves\nc. who knows all the sellers\n\n3. Let's get bun bo, which is __way spicier than pho__.\na. a local favorite\nb. famous all over Vietnam\nc. my favorite breakfast\n",
