     "md": "Level 7/unit 8/unit 8.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 8 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nTung and Irene are throwing a party at their apartment on Saturday.\nTung: OK, two days till the party. What still needs doing?\nIrene: Well, the air conditioner's broken. I'm **having it fixed** tomorrow morning.\nTung: Good. And the sofa? That wine stain is still there.\nIrene: Let's **get it cleaned** professionally. It's cheaper than you'd think.\nTung: Sounds good. Hey, did you **get your hair cut**? It looks great.\nIrene: Thanks! I **had it done** on Monday. You only noticed now?\nTung: My bad. So, are we cooking or ordering in?\nIrene: Neither. I'm **having the food catered**. We're not cooking for thirty people!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. I'm having it fixed tomorrow morning.\nlinking: “having‿it”\nchange: “fixed tomorrow” (hai âm t gộp làm một)\nstrong: “fixed”, “morning”\n“having it” nối thành “he-vin-git”. Đuôi -ed của “fixed” đọc /t/, gặp /t/ của “tomorrow” nên chỉ đọc một lần: “fiks-tơ-ma-râu”.\n\n2. It's cheaper than you'd think.\nweak: “than”, “you'd”\nstrong: “cheaper”, “think”\n“you'd” ở đây là “you would”; âm /d/ trước “think” gần như không nghe thấy: “yu-think”. “than” đọc nhẹ /ðən/ “đơn”.\n\n3. Hey, did you get your hair cut?\nchange: “did you”, “get your” (d, t + y → “j”, “ch”)\nstrong: “hair cut”\nHai lần biến âm: “did you” → “đi-jơ”, “get your” → “ghe-chơ”. Phần câu hỏi nghe như “đi-jơ-ghe-chơ-heơr-cớt”, lên giọng ở cuối.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nNhấn vào V3 (việc được làm) hơn là have / get: I'm having it FIXED.\nÂm /d/, /t/ gặp /j/ (you, your) biến thành “j”, “ch”: did you → “đi-jơ”, get your → “ghe-chơ”.\nHai âm giống nhau ở ranh giới từ chỉ đọc một lần: fixed tomorrow → “fiks-tơ-ma-râu”.\n“you'd” + động từ nguyên mẫu = you would: than you'd think → “đơn-yu-think”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**What still needs doing?**\nCòn việc gì phải làm nữa?\n“need + V-ing” mang nghĩa bị động, giống “need to be done”: The car needs washing.\nCách nói tương đương: What else do we need to do?\n\n**My bad.**\nLỗi của mình.\nCách nhận lỗi rất thân mật của người Mỹ, dùng cho lỗi nhỏ, không nghiêm trọng.\nCách nói tương đương: Sorry, my mistake.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nhave something done: nhờ hoặc thuê người khác làm\nhave + vật + V3: việc do người khác (thợ, dịch vụ) làm cho mình. Chia thì ở “have”: I'm having / I had / I'll have…\nWe [[had]] the kitchen [[painted]] last month.\nI'm [[having]] my teeth [[cleaned]] on Friday.\nShe [[has]] her nails [[done]] every week.\n\nget something done: thân mật hơn\nget + vật + V3: nghĩa giống “have”, phổ biến hơn trong văn nói. Cũng dùng cho chuyện không may xảy ra với mình (bị mất, bị hỏng…).\nYou should [[get]] that tooth [[checked]].\nI need to [[get]] my bike [[fixed]].\nShe [[got]] her bag [[stolen]] on the bus.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: OK, two days till the party. What still needs doing?\nB: Well, the air conditioner's broken. I'm having it ________ tomorrow morning.\nA: Good. And the sofa? That wine stain is still there.\nB: Let's get it cleaned professionally. It's cheaper than you'd think.\nA: Sounds good. Hey, did you get your hair cut? It looks great.\nB: Thanks! I ________ on Monday. You only noticed now?\nA: My bad. So, are we cooking or ordering in?\nB: Neither. I'm having ________. We're not cooking for thirty people!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. I'm having it __fixed__ tomorrow morning.\na. looked at\nb. serviced\nc. replaced\n\n2. I __had it done__ on Monday.\na. got it trimmed\nb. had it colored\nc. got it styled\n\n3. I'm having __the food catered__.\na. the drinks delivered\nb. a cake made\nc. the balcony decorated\n",
