     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 9 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nJonah can't find his wallet. His friend Joanna helps him retrace his steps.\nJoanna: OK, don't panic. When did you last see it?\nJonah: At lunch. I paid, so I **must have had** it then.\nJoanna: Then you **might have left** it on the table.\nJonah: No, I **can't have left** it there. I put it right back in my jacket.\nJoanna: What about the bus? It **could've slipped** out when you sat down.\nJonah: Maybe. Or someone **might have taken** it. It was so crowded.\nJoanna: Wait a second. What's that in your back pocket?\nJonah: Oh, wow. I **must have put** it there without thinking. Don't tell anyone!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. I paid, so I must have had it then.\nchange: “must have” (→ /ˈmʌstəv/)\nstrong: “paid”, “must”\n“must have” đọc nhanh thành “mớs-tơv”: “have” chỉ còn /əv/, âm /t/ nối sang. Nhấn “paid” (bằng chứng) và “must” (chắc chắn); “then” đã rõ nên đọc nhẹ.\n\n2. No, I can't have left it there.\nchange: “can't have” (→ /ˈkæntəv/)\nlinking: “left‿it”\nstrong: “can't”, “there”\nGiọng Mỹ đọc “can't” với âm /æ/ mở rộng: “ken-tơv”; còn “can” chỉ là /kən/. “left it” nối thành “lép-tit”. Nhấn “can't”: phủ định chắc chắn.\n\n3. It could've slipped out when you sat down.\nweak: “could've”\nlinking: “slipped‿out”\nchange: “sat down” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “slipped”, “sat”\n“could've” = could have, đọc “cu-đơv”. Đuôi -ed của “slipped” đọc /t/ và nối sang “out”: “slip-tao”. “sat down” mất âm /t/: “se-đaon”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nmust have / might have / could've: “have” đọc nhẹ /əv/ → “mớs-tơv”, “mai-đơv”, “cu-đơv”.\nĐuôi -ed sau /p/, /k/, /s/… đọc là /t/ và nối sang nguyên âm phía sau: slipped out → “slip-tao”.\nÂm /t/ đứng trước phụ âm thường mất: sat down → “se-đaon”.\nKhi suy đoán, nhấn vào modal để thể hiện độ chắc chắn: I MUST have…, I CAN'T have…\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**When did you last see it?**\nLần cuối bạn thấy nó là khi nào?\nCâu hỏi quen thuộc khi tìm đồ thất lạc; chú ý “last” đứng trước động từ chính.\nCách nói tương đương: When was the last time you had it?\n\n**I must have put it there without thinking.**\nChắc mình tiện tay bỏ vào đó mà không để ý.\n“without thinking” = làm theo phản xạ, theo thói quen, không suy nghĩ.\nCách nói tương đương: I must have done it on autopilot.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nmust have / can't have + V3: chắc chắn về quá khứ\nmust have + V3 = chắc chắn đã…; can't have (hoặc couldn't have) + V3 = chắc chắn đã không… Dùng khi có bằng chứng rõ ràng.\nThe lights are off. They [[must have gone]] to bed.\nShe [[can't have seen]] us. She didn't wave.\nYou [[must have been]] tired after the trip.\n\nmight / could have + V3: có lẽ đã (không chắc)\nmight / could have + V3 = có lẽ đã…, có thể đúng hoặc sai. Phủ định: might not have + V3 (có lẽ đã không…).\nHe's late. He [[might have missed]] the bus.\nI [[could have left]] my umbrella at work.\nWhere's Tom? – He [[might have gone]] home.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: OK, don't panic. When did you last see it?\nB: At lunch. I paid, so I must have had it then.\nA: Then you might have left it on the table.\nB: No, I can't have ________. I put it right back in my jacket.\nA: What about the bus? It could've slipped out when you sat down.\nB: Maybe. Or someone might have ________. It was so crowded.\nA: Wait a second. What's that in your back pocket?\nB: Oh, wow. I must have ________ without thinking. Don't tell anyone!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. No, I can't have __left it there__.\na. dropped it\nb. forgotten it\nc. lost it that fast\n\n2. Or someone might have __taken it__.\na. picked it up\nb. stolen it\nc. kicked it under a seat\n\n3. I must have __put it there__ without thinking.\na. moved it\nb. switched pockets\nc. stuck it in there\n",
