     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 10 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nNeil and Yvonne work on the same team. Yvonne is going on vacation next week.\nNeil: How's the proposal coming along? It's due on Friday.\nYvonne: Relax. **I'll have finished** the first draft by Wednesday.\nNeil: Great. And **you'll be checking** your email on vacation, right?\nYvonne: No way. This time next week, **I'll be lying** on a beach with my phone off.\nNeil: So jealous! Who'll handle the client if something comes up?\nYvonne: Kevin **will be covering** for me. **I'll have briefed** him by Thursday.\nNeil: Wow, you've really thought of everything.\nYvonne: I have. By Monday, **I'll have forgotten** this office even exists!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. I'll have finished the first draft by Wednesday.\nlinking: “I'll‿have”\nchange: “first draft” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “finished”, “Wednesday”\n“I'll have” đọc liền thành “ai-lơv”. Âm /t/ của “first” và “draft” bị nuốt trước phụ âm: /fɝs dræf baɪ/. “Wednesday” không đọc chữ “d” đầu: “wenz-đây”.\n\n2. This time next week, I'll be lying on a beach with my phone off.\nchange: “next week” (mất âm t)\nlinking: “phone‿off”\nstrong: “beach”, “off”\nÂm /t/ kẹp giữa /s/ và /w/ bị nuốt: next week → “nex-wik”. “phone off” nối thành “fâu-nóf”. Nhấn “beach” và “off” để khoe kỳ nghỉ.\n\n3. Wow, you've really thought of everything.\nchange: “thought‿of” (t → d nhẹ)\nstrong: “really”, “everything”\n“thought of” nối thành “tho-đơv”: âm /t/ giữa hai nguyên âm đọc như “d” nhẹ, “of” đọc /əv/. Nhấn “really” và “everything” để khen thật lòng.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“will have” rút gọn thành 'll have: I'll have → “ai-lơv”, we'll have → “wi-lơv”.\n“have” ở cuối câu trả lời ngắn thì đọc mạnh /hæv/: I HAVE.\nÂm /t/ kẹp giữa hai phụ âm thường bị nuốt: next week → “nex-wik”.\nTương lai tiếp diễn: “will be” đọc nhẹ, nhấn vào V-ing: I'll be LYING on a BEACH.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**How's the proposal coming along?**\nBản đề xuất tới đâu rồi?\n“come along” = tiến triển; câu hỏi tự nhiên về tiến độ công việc hay việc học.\nCách nói tương đương: How's the proposal going?\n\n**Kevin will be covering for me.**\nKevin sẽ làm thay phần việc của mình.\n“cover for someone” = làm thay việc của ai trong lúc người đó vắng mặt.\nCách nói tương đương: Kevin will be filling in for me.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nTương lai tiếp diễn: will be + V-ing\nViệc đang diễn ra tại một thời điểm trong tương lai (This time tomorrow…, At eight tonight…). Còn dùng để hỏi kế hoạch lịch sự: Will you be…?\nThis time tomorrow, [[I'll be flying]] to Tokyo.\n[[Will]] you [[be using]] the car tonight?\nAt nine, [[we'll be having]] dinner.\n\nTương lai hoàn thành: will have + V3\nViệc sẽ xong TRƯỚC một mốc trong tương lai; hay đi với by + thời gian hoặc by the time…\nBy the time we arrive, the movie [[will have started]].\nBy June, [[they'll have been]] married for ten years.\n[[Will]] you [[have finished]] by six? – Probably.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: How's the proposal coming along? It's due on Friday.\nB: Relax. I'll have ________ by Wednesday.\nA: Great. And you'll be checking your email on vacation, right?\nB: No way. This time next week, I'll be ________ with my phone off.\nA: So jealous! Who'll handle the client if something comes up?\nB: Kevin will be ________. I'll have briefed him by Thursday.\nA: Wow, you've really thought of everything.\nB: I have. By Monday, I'll have forgotten this office even exists!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. I'll have __finished the first draft__ by Wednesday.\na. checked all the numbers\nb. sent it to the team\nc. fixed the last section\n\n2. This time next week, I'll be __lying on a beach__ with my phone off.\na. hiking in the mountains\nb. relaxing by the pool\nc. snorkeling in clear water\n\n3. Kevin will be __covering for me__.\na. taking my calls\nb. handling the client\nc. running the meetings\n",
