     "md": "Level 7/unit 11/unit 11.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 11 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nWesley has two job offers. His friend Rita wants to know which one he'll take.\nRita: So, two job offers! Have you decided yet?\nWesley: Not yet. The bank pays a lot more, **although** I'd be working twelve-hour days.\nRita: Ouch. What about the other one?\nWesley: It's a small startup. **Despite** the lower salary, I'd learn so much more there.\nRita: Startups can be risky, **though**. What if it shuts down next year?\nWesley: I know. **Even though** it's risky, I'm tempted. I really clicked with the team.\nRita: Sounds like you've already made up your mind.\nWesley: Maybe. My dad prefers the bank. **However**, he won't be the one working there!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. The bank pays a lot more, although I'd be working twelve-hour days.\nchange: “lot more” (mất âm t)\nweak: “I'd be”\nstrong: “twelve-hour days”\nÂm /t/ của “lot” bị nuốt trước /m/: “ơ-la-mor”. “I'd be” = I would be, đọc lướt “ai-bi”. Nhấn “twelve-hour days” để than giờ làm quá dài.\n\n2. Startups can be risky, though.\nchange: “can be” (n → m)\nstrong: “risky”\n“can” đọc nhẹ /kən/, âm /n/ biến thành /m/ trước /b/: “cơm-bi”. “though” ở cuối câu đọc nhẹ, thấp giọng, nghĩa là “nhưng mà”.\n\n3. Even though it's risky, I'm tempted.\nchange: “tempted” (mất âm p)\nstrong: “risky”, “tempted”\n“Even though” nhấn vào “though”: “i-vơn-ĐÂU”. Âm /p/ của “tempted” kẹp giữa /m/ và /t/ nên gần như mất: “tem-tịd”. Vế đầu lên giọng nhẹ ở dấu phẩy.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“I'd” + động từ nguyên mẫu = I would (I'd be, I'd learn); “I'd” + V3 = I had.\nalthough, even though nhấn vào “though” /ðoʊ/; despite và however nhấn âm thứ hai: de-SPITE, how-EV-er.\nÂm /n/ trước /b/, /p/, /m/ dễ biến thành /m/: can be → “cơm-bi”.\nCâu nhượng bộ: vế đầu lên giọng nhẹ ở dấu phẩy, vế sau xuống giọng: Even though it's RISKY, I'm TEMPTED.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I really clicked with the team.**\nMình thấy rất hợp với cả nhóm.\n“click with someone” = hợp nhau ngay từ đầu, “hợp cạ”.\nCách nói tương đương: I really hit it off with the team.\n\n**Sounds like you've already made up your mind.**\nNghe như bạn quyết rồi đấy.\n“make up your mind” = quyết định sau khi cân nhắc. “Sounds like…” là dạng rút gọn của “It sounds like…”.\nCách nói tương đương: You've already decided, haven't you?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nalthough / even though + mệnh đề\nalthough / even though + chủ ngữ + động từ = mặc dù; even though nhấn mạnh hơn. Vế sau không thêm “but” như “mặc dù… nhưng…” trong tiếng Việt.\n[[Although]] it was late, we kept talking.\nHe kept running [[even though]] his knee hurt.\n\ndespite + danh từ / V-ing; however\ndespite + danh từ hoặc V-ing (không đi với mệnh đề). however mở đầu câu mới, sau nó là dấu phẩy; văn nói thân mật hay dùng though ở cuối câu.\n[[Despite]] the rain, the game went ahead.\n[[Despite feeling]] sick, he went to work.\nThe hotel was nice. [[However]], the food was awful.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: So, two job offers! Have you decided yet?\nB: Not yet. The bank pays a lot more, although ________.\nA: Ouch. What about the other one?\nB: It's a small startup. Despite ________, I'd learn so much more there.\nA: Startups can be risky, though. What if it shuts down next year?\nB: I know. Even though ________, I'm tempted. I really clicked with the team.\nA: Sounds like you've already made up your mind.\nB: Maybe. My dad prefers the bank. However, he won't be the one working there!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. The bank pays a lot more, although __I'd be working twelve-hour days__.\na. the commute is awful\nb. the boss seems scary\nc. I'd hardly see my family\n\n2. Despite __the lower salary__, I'd learn so much more there.\na. the long hours\nb. the tiny office\nc. earning less money\n\n3. Even though __it's risky__, I'm tempted.\na. the pay is lower\nb. my dad disagrees\nc. it might not last\n",
