     "md": "Level 7/unit 12/unit 12.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 12 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nChau and Hoang share an apartment. Their upstairs neighbor plays loud music every night.\nChau: It's two in the morning, and he's still at it!\nHoang: I can't **put up with** this anymore. I'm going up there.\nChau: Calm down. Remember last time? He **turned it down** for ten minutes, then right back up.\nHoang: Then I'll call the building manager. They can **look into** it.\nChau: Let's try to **sort it out** with him first. He's actually pretty nice.\nHoang: Nice? He **turned down** my invitation to the building barbecue.\nChau: Ha! So that's what this is really about.\nHoang: Maybe a little. Fine, I'll **bring it up** nicely. Over coffee.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. I can't put up with this anymore.\nchange: “put‿up‿with” (t → d nhẹ)\nstrong: “can't”, “anymore”\n“put up with” nối liền thành “pu-đớp-wiđ”: âm /t/ giữa hai nguyên âm đọc như “d” nhẹ. Nhấn “can't” và “anymore”: đã hết chịu nổi.\n\n2. He turned it down for ten minutes, then right back up.\nlinking: “turned‿it‿down”\nchange: “ten minutes” (n → m)\nstrong: “down”, “back up”\n“turned it down” nối liền: “tơrn-đi-đaon”. “ten minutes” → “tem-mi-nits”. Nhấn tiểu từ “down”, “back up”: chính chúng mang nghĩa.\n\n3. Let's try to sort it out with him first.\nchange: “sort‿it‿out” (t → d nhẹ)\nweak: “with him”\nstrong: “first”\nGiọng Mỹ đọc “sort it out” như “sor-đi-đao”: cả hai âm /t/ đều thành “d” nhẹ. “him” mất âm /h/: “with him” → “wi-đim”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCụm động từ tách được: tiểu từ (up, down, out) thường được nhấn: turn it DOWN, bring it UP.\nĐại từ “it” ở giữa đọc rất nhẹ và nối hai bên: sort it out → “sor-đi-đao”.\nÂm /t/ giữa hai nguyên âm đọc như “d” nhẹ: put up → “pu-đớp”.\nÂm /n/ trước /m/, /p/, /b/ biến thành /m/: ten minutes → “tem-mi-nits”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**It's two in the morning, and he's still at it!**\nHai giờ sáng rồi mà anh ta vẫn chưa chịu thôi!\n“be still at it” = vẫn đang làm việc gì đó (thường kéo dài, gây khó chịu).\nCách nói tương đương: He's still going!\n\n**So that's what this is really about.**\nÀ, hóa ra đây mới là lý do thật.\nDùng khi phát hiện ra động cơ thật đằng sau lời phàn nàn hay hành động của ai đó.\nCách nói tương đương: So that's the real reason!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nCụm động từ tách được: turn down, sort out, bring up…\nDanh từ đứng trước hay sau tiểu từ đều được: turn the music down / turn down the music. Đại từ (it, him…) phải đứng giữa: turn it down, không nói turn down it.\nCould you [[turn]] the TV [[down]]?\nShe [[turned down]] the job offer.\nDon't worry, I'll [[sort it out]].\n\nCụm động từ không tách được: look into, put up with, deal with…\nTân ngữ, kể cả đại từ, luôn đứng sau cả cụm: look into it, put up with him; không chen vào giữa.\nThe police are [[looking into]] the case.\nHow do you [[put up with]] him?\nI'll [[deal with]] it tomorrow.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: It's two in the morning, and he's still at it!\nB: I can't ________ this anymore. I'm going up there.\nA: Calm down. Remember last time? He turned it down for ten minutes, then right back up.\nB: Then I'll call the building manager. They can ________.\nA: Let's try to sort it out with him first. He's actually pretty nice.\nB: Nice? He turned down my invitation to the building barbecue.\nA: Ha! So that's what this is really about.\nB: Maybe a little. Fine, I'll ________ nicely. Over coffee.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. I can't __put up with__ this anymore.\na. deal with\nb. cope with\nc. stand\n\n2. They can __look into it__.\na. check it out\nb. sort it out\nc. have a word with him\n\n3. Fine, I'll __bring it up__ nicely.\na. point it out\nb. mention it\nc. ask him\n",
