     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 2 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nBridget's presentation to a new client didn't go well. Her colleague Caleb tries to cheer her up.\nCaleb: Chin up. It **could have been** a lot worse, you know.\nBridget: Worse? My laptop froze twice! I **should have brought** a backup.\nCaleb: True. And maybe you **shouldn't have crammed** in all thirty slides.\nBridget: Don't remind me. I **could have skipped** the whole intro, honestly.\nCaleb: Still, your answer on pricing was spot on. They looked properly impressed.\nBridget: Really? Then I **should have started** with that!\nCaleb: Exactly. Lead with the numbers next time, and keep the rest short.\nBridget: Good tip. You **could have told** me that before I went in, though!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. I should have brought a backup.\nchange: “should have” (đọc thành “shoulda”)\nlinking: “brought‿a”\nstrong: “backup”\n“should have” nói nhanh thành “shoulda” /ˈʃʊdə/ “shu-đơ”: âm /h/ và /v/ gần như mất. “brought a” nối thành “bro-đơ” (giọng Mỹ, t → d nhẹ).\n\n2. It could have been a lot worse, you know.\nweak: “could have been”\nstrong: “lot”, “worse”\n“could have been” lướt thành “cu-đơ-bin”, “been” đọc nhẹ /bɪn/. Giọng Anh: /t/ của “lot” thường bị nuốt trước “worse”; “worse” không có /r/: /wɜːs/ “wơơs”.\n\n3. You could have told me that before I went in, though!\nweak: “could have”\nlinking: “went‿in”\nstrong: “before”\nNhấn mạnh “before” (lẽ ra phải nói trước, chứ không phải bây giờ) để trách đùa. “went in” nối thành “wen-nin”: giọng Mỹ hay bỏ /t/ sau /n/.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nshould have, could have, would have nói nhanh thành “shoulda”, “coulda”, “woulda” /ˈʃʊdə/, /ˈkʊdə/, /ˈwʊdə/.\nĐây chỉ là cách nói; khi viết vẫn dùng should have hoặc should've.\nTrong câu tiếc nuối, “should have” đọc nhẹ, nhấn vào thông tin chính: I should have brought a BACKUP.\nNhấn một từ để đối lập (BEFORE, chứ không phải bây giờ) giúp lời trách nghe vui, không nặng nề.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Don't remind me.**\nĐừng nhắc nữa (mình biết rồi).\nĐáp lại khi người kia nhắc tới một chuyện không hay mà mình đã biết và không muốn nghĩ tới nữa.\nCách nói tương đương: I know, I know.\n\n**Your answer on pricing was spot on.**\nCâu trả lời của bạn về giá cả rất chuẩn.\n“spot on” (kiểu Anh) là hoàn toàn chính xác. “properly” ở câu sau cũng là cách nói của người Anh, nghĩa là “thật sự”.\nCách nói tương đương: Your answer on pricing was perfect.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nshould have / shouldn't have + V3: tiếc nuối, trách\nLẽ ra nên làm mà đã không làm, hoặc lẽ ra không nên làm mà đã làm. Dùng để tiếc cho mình hoặc trách nhẹ người khác.\nI [[should have saved]] the file first.\nYou [[shouldn't have stayed]] up so late.\nWe [[should have left]] home earlier.\n\ncould have + V3: lẽ ra đã có thể\nMột khả năng trong quá khứ nhưng đã không xảy ra. “You could have + V3” còn dùng để trách nhẹ: bạn đã có thể làm vậy mà lại không làm.\nWe [[could have taken]] a taxi, but we walked.\nYou [[could have called]] me! I was worried.\nSlow down! You [[could have hit]] that cyclist.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Chin up. It could have been a lot worse, you know.\nB: Worse? My laptop froze twice! I should have ________.\nA: True. And maybe you shouldn't have crammed in all thirty slides.\nB: Don't remind me. I could have ________, honestly.\nA: Still, your answer on pricing was spot on. They looked properly impressed.\nB: Really? Then I should have started with that!\nA: Exactly. Lead with the numbers next time, and keep the rest short.\nB: Good tip. You could have ________ before I went in, though!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. I should have __brought a backup__.\na. tested everything first\nb. printed the slides\nc. arrived a bit earlier\n\n2. I could have __skipped the whole intro__, honestly.\na. cut the history part\nb. dropped half the slides\nc. kept it much shorter\n\n3. You could have __told me that__ before I went in, though!\na. mentioned it\nb. warned me\nc. said something\n",
