     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 4 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nIn a team meeting, Edward and Eleanor discuss a new policy on working from home.\nEdward: So, management wants us in the office three days a week. Thoughts?\nEleanor: **If you ask me**, it's a step backward. We're more productive at home.\nEdward: **I see what you mean, but** we've barely seen each other for months.\nEleanor: **That's a fair point.** Our video calls can feel a bit flat.\nEdward: **The way I see it**, some time together would do us good.\nEleanor: **I'm not so sure about** three, though. Some of us live over an hour away.\nEdward: Fair enough. Shall we propose two, then, and let people choose?\nEleanor: **I couldn't agree more.** Let's run it by management.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. If you ask me, it's a step backward.\nweak: “you”, “a”\nlinking: “it's‿a”\nstrong: “ask”, “backward”\nĐọc liền “If you ask me” rồi ngừng ngắn. Giọng Mỹ đọc “ask” /æsk/ “ésk”, giọng Anh đọc /ɑːsk/ “aask”. “it's a” nối thành “it-sơ”.\n\n2. I see what you mean, but we've barely seen each other for months.\nchange: “what‿you” (t + y → “ch”)\nweak: “but”\nstrong: “mean”, “months”\nGiọng xuống rồi hơi lên ở “mean” (lịch sự, báo hiệu sắp nói ý khác), ngừng ngắn trước “but”. “what you” đọc thành “wo-chu”.\n\n3. I'm not so sure about three, though.\nlinking: “sure‿about”\nstrong: “three”\nNhấn “three” (chỉ phản đối con số, không phản đối cả ý). “though” xuống rồi hơi lên cho lời phản đối mềm hơn. “sure about” nối âm /r/: “shua-rơ-bao”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nPhản đối lịch sự: giọng xuống rồi hơi lên ở cuối cụm (I see what you mean… / …though), không xuống hẳn.\nNhấn vào đúng từ mình muốn bàn lại: not so sure about THREE.\nCụm mở đầu (If you ask me, The way I see it) đọc liền một hơi rồi ngừng ngắn.\nGiọng Anh và giọng Mỹ khác nhau ở “ask”, “can't”: /ɑː/ (Anh) và /æ/ (Mỹ).\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Thoughts?**\nMọi người thấy sao?\nCách hỏi ý kiến ngắn gọn, thân mật trong cuộc họp, ngay sau khi nêu một vấn đề.\nCách nói tương đương: What does everyone think?\n\n**Let's run it by management.**\nMình trình ý này lên ban quản lý xem sao.\n“run something by someone” là hỏi ý kiến hoặc xin ai đó duyệt trước khi quyết định.\nCách nói tương đương: Let's check with management.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nNêu ý kiến: If you ask me / The way I see it / In my view\nĐặt ở đầu câu để báo đây là ý kiến riêng, nghe mềm hơn nói thẳng. “If you ask me” thân mật; “In my view” trang trọng hơn.\n[[If you ask me]], the movie was too long.\n[[The way I see it]], we need more staff.\n[[In my view]], the price is a little high.\n\nĐồng ý và phản đối lịch sự\nĐồng ý hoàn toàn: I couldn't agree more. Đồng ý một phần: That's a fair point. Phản đối nhẹ nhàng: I see what you mean, but… / I'm not so sure about…\nWe need a break. – [[I couldn't agree more]].\n[[I see what you mean, but]] it's too risky.\n[[I'm not so sure about]] the new logo.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: So, management wants us in the office three days a week. Thoughts?\nB: ________, it's a step backward. We're more productive at home.\nA: I see what you mean, but we've barely seen each other for months.\nB: ________. Our video calls can feel a bit flat.\nA: The way I see it, some time together would do us good.\nB: ________ three, though. Some of us live over an hour away.\nA: Fair enough. Shall we propose two, then, and let people choose?\nB: I couldn't agree more. Let's run it by management.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. __If you ask me__, it's a step backward.\na. Personally\nb. In my opinion\nc. To be honest\n\n2. __That's a fair point__. Our video calls can feel a bit flat.\na. Good point\nb. That's true\nc. You've got a point there\n\n3. __I'm not so sure about__ three, though.\na. I'm a bit worried about\nb. I have my doubts about\nc. I'm not sold on\n",
