     "md": "Level 8/unit 5/unit 5.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 5 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nKhai wants to open a café near a university. He asks his friend Freya, who runs a bakery, for feedback.\nKhai: OK, be honest. What do you think of my café plan?\nFreya: Well, I love the idea. **It might be a bit** ambitious, though.\nKhai: Ambitious? In what way?\nFreya: Ninety seats **seems like quite a lot** for your first café. **Perhaps you could** start smaller?\nKhai: Point taken. What about the prices? Don't hold back.\nFreya: They're **possibly a touch** on the high side for a student area.\nKhai: So basically, you think it's a terrible idea.\nFreya: Not at all! **I'd just** tweak a few things. And I'll be your first customer.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. It might be a bit ambitious, though.\nweak: “a bit”\nlinking: “bit‿ambitious”\nstrong: “ambitious”\n“bit ambitious” nối thành “bi-tam-bi-shợs”; giọng Anh giữ /t/ rõ. “though” cuối câu xuống rồi hơi lên: lời chê nghe mềm hẳn.\n\n2. Ninety seats seems like quite a lot for your first café.\nlinking: “quite‿a‿lot”\nweak: “for your”\nstrong: “Ninety”, “first”\nGiọng Anh giữ /t/ rõ: “Ninety” /ˈnaɪnti/ “nai-nti”, “quite a lot” nối thành “quai-tơ-lot”. Giọng Mỹ hay đọc “nai-ni”, “quai-đơ-lat”.\n\n3. Not at all! I'd just tweak a few things.\nlinking: “Not‿at‿all”\nchange: “just tweak” (hai âm t gộp làm một)\nstrong: “all”, “few”\n“Not at all” nối thành “no-tơ-tôl” (giọng Mỹ: “na-đơ-đal”). Trong “just tweak”, hai âm /t/ gộp làm một: “jớs-twik”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nTừ rào đón (a bit, possibly, perhaps) đọc nhẹ, không nhấn; nhấn vào ý chính: a bit AMBITIOUS.\nLời góp ý kết thúc bằng “though” hoặc câu hỏi (Perhaps you could…?) thường xuống rồi hơi lên: nghe mềm, không áp đặt.\nGiọng Anh (Freya) giữ /t/ rõ giữa hai nguyên âm: not at all → “no-tơ-tôl”; giọng Mỹ (Khai) đọc thành “d” nhẹ.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Don't hold back.**\nCứ nói thẳng đi, đừng ngại.\nDùng khi muốn người kia góp ý thật lòng, kể cả điều khó nghe. “hold back” là kìm lại, không nói hết.\nCách nói tương đương: Give it to me straight.\n\n**They're possibly a touch on the high side for a student area.**\nGiá có lẽ hơi cao một chút so với khu sinh viên.\n“on the high side” là hơi cao; “a touch” (kiểu Anh) là một chút. Cả hai làm lời chê nhẹ đi nhiều.\nCách nói tương đương: They might be a little high for students.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nNói giảm: might / seem / a bit / slightly\nThêm từ rào đón để lời nhận xét bớt nặng nề: dùng might, could thay cho is; seem thay cho be; thêm a bit, slightly, a little trước tính từ.\nThe plan [[might be a bit]] risky.\nThis soup [[seems slightly]] salty to me.\nYour speech [[could be a little]] shorter.\n\nGóp ý mềm mỏng: Perhaps you could… / I'd just… / I wonder if…\nĐưa lời khuyên như một gợi ý, không phải mệnh lệnh. “I'd + V” nghĩa là “nếu là tôi thì tôi sẽ…”; “I wonder if…” rất lịch sự.\n[[Perhaps you could]] ask your manager first?\n[[I'd just]] change the title a little.\n[[I wonder if]] a bigger font [[might]] help.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: OK, be honest. What do you think of my café plan?\nB: Well, I love the idea. It might be ________, though.\nA: Ambitious? In what way?\nB: Ninety seats seems like quite a lot for your first café. Perhaps you could ________?\nA: Point taken. What about the prices? Don't hold back.\nB: They're possibly a touch on the high side for a student area.\nA: So basically, you think it's a terrible idea.\nB: Not at all! I'd just ________. And I'll be your first customer.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. It might be __a bit ambitious__, though.\na. slightly risky\nb. a little expensive\nc. a tad optimistic\n\n2. Perhaps you could __start smaller__?\na. open with fifty seats\nb. rent a smaller place\nc. test the idea first\n\n3. I'd just __tweak a few things__.\na. rethink the location\nb. shorten the menu a little\nc. lower the prices slightly\n",
