     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 6 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nHeidi heard that Frank criticized her project at yesterday's meeting. She wants to talk to him about it.\nHeidi: Frank, got a minute? I heard you called my project a disaster.\nFrank: Hang on. **What I said was** that the deadline was a disaster.\nHeidi: Really? Because that's not how it came across.\nFrank: Honestly, **it's the client who** keeps changing the brief, not you.\nHeidi: Then why did Jake say you were annoyed with me?\nFrank: Jake got the wrong end of the stick. **What annoyed me was** all the last-minute changes.\nHeidi: OK. But **what really hurt was** hearing it from someone else.\nFrank: That's fair. Sorry. Next time, I'll come straight to you.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. What I said was that the deadline was a disaster.\nlinking: “What‿I”\nweak: “was”, “that”\nstrong: “said”, “deadline”\nNhấn mạnh “deadline” để sửa lại ý (hạn chót, chứ không phải dự án). “What I” nối thành “wo-tai”: giọng Anh giữ /t/, giọng Mỹ đọc “wa-đai”.\n\n2. Honestly, it's the client who keeps changing the brief, not you.\nweak: “who”\nstrong: “client”, “you”\nCâu chẻ “it's… who…” đặt từ cần nhấn (client) vào giữa câu; nhấn “client” và “you” để đối lập. Ngắt nhẹ trước “not you”. Chữ “h” trong “Honestly” câm.\n\n3. But what really hurt was hearing it from someone else.\nlinking: “hearing‿it”, “someone‿else”\nstrong: “hurt”, “else”\nLên giọng nhẹ ở “hurt” và ngừng ngắn, rồi mới nói ý chính. “hearing it” nối thành “hia-ring-it”; “someone else” thành “sơm-wơ-nels”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCâu chẻ chia hai phần: phần “What I said was…” lên giọng nhẹ và ngừng ngắn, rồi nhấn ý chính ở phần sau.\nKhi sửa hiểu lầm, nhấn mạnh từ mang ý đối lập: the DEADLINE (không phải the project), the CLIENT (không phải you).\nGiọng Anh (Frank) giữ /t/ rõ: What I → “wo-tai”; giọng Mỹ (Heidi) đọc “wa-đai”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Jake got the wrong end of the stick.**\nJake hiểu nhầm rồi.\nThành ngữ hay dùng ở Anh: hiểu sai hoàn toàn ý của người khác.\nCách nói tương đương: Jake misunderstood.\n\n**Next time, I'll come straight to you.**\nLần sau có gì tôi sẽ nói trực tiếp với bạn.\n“come straight to someone” là tìm gặp và nói thẳng với chính người đó, không để họ nghe lại qua người khác.\nCách nói tương đương: Next time, I'll talk to you directly.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nCâu chẻ với What: What + mệnh đề + is/was…\nĐưa phần quan trọng ra sau “is/was” để nhấn mạnh hoặc sửa lại ý. Hay gặp: What I meant was…, What I need is…, What surprised me was…\n[[What I meant was]] that I need more time.\n[[What I need is]] a good night's sleep.\n[[What surprised me was]] how cheap it was.\n\nCâu chẻ với It: It is/was + X + who/that…\nNhấn mạnh người hoặc vật X đã làm việc gì, thường để sửa một thông tin sai. Dùng who cho người, that cho vật.\n[[It was Mai who]] booked the hotel, not me.\n[[It's the noise that]] bothers me, not the heat.\n[[Was it you who]] called me last night?\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Frank, got a minute? I heard you called my project a disaster.\nB: Hang on. What I said was that ________.\nA: Really? Because that's not how it came across.\nB: Honestly, it's the client who ________, not you.\nA: Then why did Jake say you were annoyed with me?\nB: Jake got the wrong end of the stick. What annoyed me was ________.\nA: OK. But what really hurt was hearing it from someone else.\nB: That's fair. Sorry. Next time, I'll come straight to you.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. What I said was that __the deadline was a disaster__.\na. the timing was awful\nb. we needed more help\nc. the budget was too tight\n\n2. Honestly, it's the client who __keeps changing the brief__, not you.\na. keeps moving the goalposts\nb. can't make up their mind\nc. wants everything yesterday\n\n3. What annoyed me was __all the last-minute changes__.\na. the lack of support\nb. the endless emails\nc. the way it was planned\n",
