     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 7 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nHong just got back from a trip to Lisbon. Her friend George wants to hear all about it.\nGeorge: Hey, welcome back! So, how was Lisbon? Tell me everything.\nHong: Amazing, mostly. But on the first night, I got locked out of the flat.\nGeorge: Oh no! How on earth did that happen?\nHong: I **was taking** the rubbish out when the door **slammed** shut behind me.\nGeorge: Let me guess. **You'd left** your keys inside?\nHong: Keys, phone, everything. And **I'd already changed** into my pyjamas!\nGeorge: That's hilarious. Sorry! So how did you get back in?\nHong: Luckily, a neighbour **was walking** her dog, so I borrowed her phone and called the owner.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. I was taking the rubbish out when the door slammed shut behind me.\nweak: “was”, “the”\nlinking: “rubbish‿out”\nstrong: “rubbish”, “slammed shut”\nNgắt hai cụm: “I was taking the rubbish out” / “when the door slammed shut behind me”. “was” đọc nhẹ /wəz/. “rubbish out” nối thành “rơ-bi-shao”.\n\n2. And I'd already changed into my pyjamas!\nlinking: “I'd‿already”\nstrong: “pyjamas”\n“I'd” ở đây là “I had”; “I'd already” nối thành “ai-đol-re-đi”. “pyjamas” (Mỹ: pajamas) /pəˈdʒɑːməz/ “pơ-ja-mơz”: nhấn, kéo dài âm giữa để gây cười.\n\n3. So how did you get back in?\nchange: “did‿you” (d + y → j)\nlinking: “back‿in”\nstrong: “in”\n“did you” biến âm thành “đi-jơ”; “back in” nối thành “bé-kin”. Tiểu từ “in” của “get back in” được nhấn ở cuối câu.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nKhi kể chuyện, ngắt câu dài theo ý: bối cảnh (I was taking…) / sự việc chen ngang (when the door…).\nNhấn và kéo dài chi tiết bất ngờ (slammed shut, pyjamas) để câu chuyện hấp dẫn hơn.\nGiọng Anh (Hong) không đọc /r/ cuối âm tiết: door → “đo”; giọng Mỹ (George) đọc “đor”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**How on earth did that happen?**\nLàm sao mà lại thế được?\n“on earth” đặt sau từ để hỏi (how, what, why) để nhấn mạnh sự ngạc nhiên.\nCách nói tương đương: How did that even happen?\n\n**I got locked out of the flat.**\nMình bị kẹt ở ngoài, không vào lại căn hộ được.\n“get locked out (of)” là bị khoá cửa ở ngoài, không vào được. “flat” là cách nói của người Anh (Mỹ: apartment).\nCách nói tương đương: I couldn't get back into the apartment.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nQuá khứ tiếp diễn + when + quá khứ đơn\nQuá khứ tiếp diễn tả bối cảnh, việc đang diễn ra; quá khứ đơn tả sự việc chen ngang. Dùng while trước việc đang diễn ra.\n[[I was cooking]] when the lights [[went]] out.\n[[While we were hiking]], it [[started]] to snow.\n\nQuá khứ hoàn thành: had + V3\nDiễn tả việc đã xảy ra trước một việc khác trong quá khứ. Hay đi với already, just, by the time.\nThe train [[had already left]] when we [[arrived]].\n[[I'd forgotten]] my passport, so I [[missed]] the flight.\n[[By the time]] he called, [[I'd gone]] to bed.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Hey, welcome back! So, how was Lisbon? Tell me everything.\nB: Amazing, mostly. But on the first night, I got locked out of the flat.\nA: Oh no! How on earth did that happen?\nB: I was taking ________ when the door slammed shut behind me.\nA: Let me guess. You'd left your keys inside?\nB: Keys, phone, everything. And I'd already ________!\nA: That's hilarious. Sorry! So how did you get back in?\nB: Luckily, a neighbour was ________, so I borrowed her phone and called the owner.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. I was taking __the rubbish out__ when the door slammed shut behind me.\na. a photo of the view\nb. the washing in\nc. a call outside\n\n2. And I'd already __changed into my pyjamas__!\na. taken my contacts out\nb. washed my hair\nc. had two glasses of wine\n\n3. Luckily, a neighbour was __walking her dog__, so I borrowed her phone and called the owner.\na. coming home\nb. putting her bins out\nc. sitting outside\n",
