     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 8 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nLam rents a house from Ingrid. She wants to raise the rent next year, so they're negotiating.\nIngrid: Lam, I'm afraid I'll have to raise your rent by ten percent next year.\nLam: Ten percent? That's quite steep. **What if** I **signed** for two years instead?\nIngrid: That would help. I could probably do seven, then.\nLam: I was rather hoping for three. Could we **meet halfway** at five?\nIngrid: You drive a hard bargain! Five it is, **as long as** you mow the lawn.\nLam: Happy to, **provided that** the boiler gets fixed before winter.\nIngrid: That's reasonable. I'll have it looked at on Monday.\nLam: Brilliant. Then I think we've got a deal.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. What if I signed for two years instead?\nlinking: “What‿if‿I”\nweak: “for”\nstrong: “two years”, “instead”\n“What if I” nối thành “wo-ti-phai” (giọng Anh giữ /t/; giọng Mỹ đọc “wa-đi-phai”). “for” đọc nhẹ /fə/. Lên giọng nhẹ ở cuối: đề xuất mang tính thăm dò.\n\n2. Could we meet halfway at five?\nweak: “Could we”\nstrong: “halfway”, “five”\nChữ “l” trong “half” câm: giọng Anh đọc /ˌhɑːfˈweɪ/ “haaf-wây”, giọng Mỹ /ˌhæfˈweɪ/ “hép-wây”. Nhấn “five”: con số mình đề xuất.\n\n3. Happy to, provided that the boiler gets fixed before winter.\nweak: “that”\nchange: “fixed” (đuôi -ed đọc /t/)\nstrong: “boiler”, “winter”\nNgắt nhẹ sau “Happy to”. “that” đọc nhẹ /ðət/; “fixed” đọc /fɪkst/. Giọng Anh: “winter” “win-tơ”; giọng Mỹ hay bỏ /t/: “wi-nơr”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nKhi thương lượng, nhấn vào con số và điều kiện: meet halfway at FIVE, provided that the BOILER…\nCâu đề xuất “What if…?”, “Could we…?” lên giọng nhẹ ở cuối để nghe mềm mỏng, còn chỗ để bàn.\n“that” trong “provided that” đọc nhẹ /ðət/, có thể bỏ hẳn: provided the boiler…\nGiọng Anh đọc half, rather với /ɑː/ (“haaf”, “raa-đơ”); giọng Mỹ đọc /æ/ (“hép”, “re-đơr”).\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**You drive a hard bargain!**\nAnh mặc cả giỏi thật đấy!\nNói khi đối phương thương lượng cứng rắn, khó nhượng bộ; thường nửa đùa nửa thật.\nCách nói tương đương: You're a tough negotiator!\n\n**Five it is.**\nVậy chốt năm phần trăm nhé.\n“… it is” dùng để chốt một lựa chọn sau khi bàn bạc.\nCách nói tương đương: OK, let's go with five.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nĐưa đề xuất: What if…? / meet halfway\n“What if + quá khứ đơn?” đưa ra đề xuất một cách thăm dò, mềm hơn dùng hiện tại đơn. “meet (someone) halfway” là mỗi bên nhượng bộ một nửa.\n[[What if]] we [[paid]] in two parts?\n[[What if]] I [[worked]] from home on Fridays?\nYou say fifty, I say thirty. [[Shall we meet halfway]]?\n\nĐặt điều kiện: provided that / as long as\nCả hai nghĩa là “với điều kiện là”, theo sau là hiện tại đơn dù nói về tương lai. “provided (that)” trang trọng hơn “as long as”.\nYou can borrow it, [[as long as]] you [[bring]] it back.\nWe'll deliver free, [[provided that]] you [[order]] before noon.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: Lam, I'm afraid I'll have to raise your rent by ten percent next year.\nB: Ten percent? That's quite steep. What if I ________ instead?\nA: That would help. I could probably do seven, then.\nB: I was rather hoping for three. Could we ________ at five?\nA: You drive a hard bargain! Five it is, as long as you mow the lawn.\nB: Happy to, provided that ________ before winter.\nA: That's reasonable. I'll have it looked at on Monday.\nB: Brilliant. Then I think we've got a deal.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. What if I __signed for two years__ instead?\na. paid six months upfront\nb. signed a longer lease\nc. did some repairs myself\n\n2. Could we __meet halfway__ at five?\na. settle\nb. compromise\nc. meet in the middle\n\n3. Happy to, provided that __the boiler gets fixed__ before winter.\na. the heating is sorted\nb. you fix the windows\nc. the roof is repaired\n",
