     "md": "Level 8/unit 11/unit 11.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 11 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nSelena checked into her hotel an hour ago. Now she's back at the front desk, talking to Liam.\nSelena: **Sorry to bother you, but** there's a problem with my room.\nLiam: **I'm sorry to hear that.** What seems to be the trouble?\nSelena: The air conditioning **doesn't seem to** work, and it's rather hot.\nLiam: **I do apologize.** I'll have someone take a look right away.\nSelena: Thank you. Also, **I was wondering if** I could change rooms. It's a bit noisy.\nLiam: Of course. **Let me see what I can do.** How about the top floor?\nSelena: That would be lovely. Sorry to be such a pain.\nLiam: Not at all. And breakfast is on us tomorrow, to make up for it.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. Sorry to bother you, but there's a problem with my room.\nweak: “to”, “but”\nlinking: “there's‿a”\nstrong: “problem”, “room”\nGiọng xuống rồi hơi lên ở “bother you” (lịch sự, báo trước lời phàn nàn), ngừng ngắn. “there's a” nối thành “đe-zơ”; giọng Anh không đọc /r/: /ðeəz/.\n\n2. I do apologize.\nstrong: “do”\n“do” được nhấn mạnh để lời xin lỗi nghe chân thành hơn (đây không phải câu hỏi). “apologize” nhấn âm thứ hai: /əˈpɑːlədʒaɪz/ “ơ-pa-lơ-jaiz”.\n\n3. Also, I was wondering if I could change rooms.\nweak: “was”, “could”\nlinking: “wondering‿if‿I”\nstrong: “change rooms”\n“was”, “could” đọc nhẹ /wəz/, /kəd/. “wondering if I” nối thành “wan-đơ-ri-ngi-phai”. Giọng xuống rồi hơi lên ở “rooms”: lời đề nghị nghe khiêm tốn.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nPhàn nàn lịch sự: nói chậm, giọng nhẹ, xuống rồi hơi lên ở cuối cụm (bother you…, change rooms…), không xuống giọng gắt.\nMuốn lời xin lỗi chân thành hơn, nhấn mạnh trợ động từ: I DO apologize.\nTrong câu đề nghị, các từ nhỏ đọc nhẹ: I was wondering if I could… → “ai-wơz-wan-đơ-ri-ngi-phai-cơd”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**What seems to be the trouble?**\nQuý khách gặp vấn đề gì ạ?\nCâu hỏi lịch sự của nhân viên khi khách báo có sự cố; “seems to be” làm câu hỏi nhẹ nhàng hơn.\nCách nói tương đương: What's the problem?\n\n**Sorry to be such a pain.**\nXin lỗi đã làm phiền anh nhiều quá.\n“be a pain” (thân mật) là gây phiền phức, làm mất công người khác. Hay nói sau khi đã nhờ vả hoặc phàn nàn nhiều.\nCách nói tương đương: Sorry for all the trouble.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nPhàn nàn khéo léo\nMở đầu bằng lời xin lỗi (Sorry to bother you, but…), dùng “seem to” cho nhẹ bớt, và dùng câu gián tiếp (I was wondering if…) thay cho đòi hỏi.\n[[Sorry to bother you, but]] my key doesn't work.\nThe shower [[doesn't seem to]] be working.\n[[I was wondering if]] I could get a refund.\n\nĐáp lại lời phàn nàn\nThể hiện sự cảm thông, xin lỗi, rồi đưa ra giải pháp. “I'll have someone + V” nghĩa là tôi sẽ cho người đến làm việc gì đó.\n[[I'm so sorry about that]]. It won't happen again.\n[[I'll have someone]] bring up fresh towels.\n[[I'll look into it]] right away.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Sorry to bother you, but there's a problem with my room.\nB: ________. What seems to be the trouble?\nA: The air conditioning doesn't seem to work, and it's rather hot.\nB: I do apologize. I'll have someone ________ right away.\nA: Thank you. Also, I was wondering if I could change rooms. It's a bit noisy.\nB: Of course. Let me see what I can do. How about the top floor?\nA: That would be lovely. Sorry to be such a pain.\nB: Not at all. And ________ is on us tomorrow, to make up for it.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. __I'm sorry to hear that__. What seems to be the trouble?\na. Oh dear\nb. I'm so sorry\nc. That's not good\n\n2. I'll have someone __take a look__ right away.\na. fix it\nb. bring you a fan\nc. check the unit\n\n3. And __breakfast__ is on us tomorrow, to make up for it.\na. dinner\nb. the spa\nc. room service\n",
