     "md": "Level 9/unit 1/unit 1.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 1 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nAmber and Alfie are walking home after dinner at a tiny seafood restaurant.\nAmber: Right, I'm calling it. Best meal of the year.\nAlfie: No argument here. **Never have I** had scallops that good.\nAmber: And the service! **Not once did** we have to flag anyone down.\nAlfie: Right? And **not only was** the food amazing, but the prices were fair, too.\nAmber: Thirty quid a head! How did you even find this place?\nAlfie: Total fluke. I ducked in to get out of the rain.\nAmber: Well, **little did you know** you'd struck gold.\nAlfie: Listen to us. We sound like a couple of food critics.\nAmber: Speak for yourself! Next time, we're trying the crab.\nAlfie: Deal. And **no way am I** sharing it.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. Never have I had scallops that good.\nweak: “have I”\nstrong: “Never”, “scallops”, “good”\nĐảo ngữ: dồn trọng âm vào từ phủ định đứng đầu câu. Trợ động từ “have” đọc yếu, nối với “I” thành “hơ-vai”.\n\n2. Not once did we have to flag anyone down.\nstrong: “Not once”, “down”\nchange: “have to” (v → f)\nlinking: “flag‿anyone”\n“Not once” đọc chậm và mạnh. “have to” (phải) đọc /ˈhæftə/ “háf-tơ”. “flag anyone” nối thành “fla-ghe-ni-wơn”.\n\n3. And no way am I sharing it.\nlinking: “am‿I”\nstrong: “no way”, “sharing”\nNói đùa nhưng dứt khoát: “no way” đọc chậm, mạnh; “am I” lướt nhanh thành “ơ-mai”. Xuống giọng ở cuối câu.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCâu đảo ngữ: nhấn từ phủ định đầu câu (NEVER, NOT ONCE, NO WAY); trợ động từ theo sau đọc nhẹ.\n“have to” mang nghĩa “phải” đọc /ˈhæftə/, “has to” đọc /ˈhæstə/.\nGiọng Anh (Amber) thường không đọc r cuối từ: year → /jɪə/; giọng Mỹ (Alfie) đọc rõ: never → /ˈnevɚ/.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Total fluke.**\nHoàn toàn là may mắn thôi.\n“fluke” là chuyện may mắn tình cờ, không hề tính trước; cũng hay dùng để khiêm tốn khi được khen.\nCách nói tương đương: Pure luck.\n\n**Speak for yourself!**\nBạn thì có, chứ mình thì không nhé!\nCâu đáp vui khi người kia nói “chúng ta” mà mình không muốn bị tính vào.\nCách nói tương đương: That's just you!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nĐảo ngữ sau từ phủ định: Never / Not once / No way\nTừ phủ định đứng đầu câu thì trợ động từ đảo lên trước chủ ngữ, giống câu hỏi. Dùng để nhấn mạnh cảm xúc, văn nói hay dùng khi đùa.\n[[Never have I]] seen such a beautiful sunset.\n[[Not once did]] he say thank you.\n[[No way am I]] paying for that.\n\nNot only… but (also)… / Little did I know…\n“Not only” và “Little” đứng đầu câu cũng kéo theo đảo ngữ. “Little did I / you know” = lúc đó hoàn toàn không biết, hay dùng khi kể chuyện.\n[[Not only is]] it cheap, [[but]] it's [[also]] really quick.\n[[Little did we know]] the storm was heading our way.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: Right, I'm calling it. Best meal of the year.\nB: No argument here. Never have I ________.\nA: And the service! Not once did we have to flag anyone down.\nB: Right? And not only was the food amazing, but ________, too.\nA: Thirty quid a head! How did you even find this place?\nB: Total fluke. I ducked in to get out of the rain.\nA: Well, little did you know you'd struck gold.\nB: Listen to us. We sound like a couple of food critics.\nA: Speak for yourself! Next time, we're trying the crab.\nB: Deal. And no way am I ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. Never have I __had scallops that good__.\na. tasted bread like that\nb. enjoyed a meal more\nc. eaten so much\n\n2. And not only was the food amazing, but __the prices were fair__, too.\na. the view was stunning\nb. the portions were huge\nc. the music was perfect\n\n3. And no way am I __sharing it__.\na. letting you pay\nb. skipping dessert\nc. ordering anything else\n",
