     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 3 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nCora rushes over to Conor's desk with some office gossip.\nCora: Have you heard? Apparently we're being bought out!\nConor: I've heard the rumors. The buyer **is thought to be** our biggest rival.\nCora: Them? The ones who keep poaching our clients?\nConor: Allegedly. And the deal **is expected to be** announced next month.\nCora: Great. So should I start updating my CV?\nConor: Not yet. Their CEO **is said to have** kept everyone on last time.\nCora: Last time? So they've done this before?\nConor: Twice. They're **supposed to be** pretty decent employers, actually.\nCora: Well, that's a relief. How do you know all this?\nConor: Let's just say the walls in this building are very thin.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. The buyer is thought to be our biggest rival.\nweak: “is”, “to be”\nlinking: “thought‿to”\nstrong: “buyer”, “biggest rival”\n“thought to” chỉ đọc một âm t: “thót-tơ”. Cụm “is thought to be” đọc lướt; nhấn vào tin chính: “biggest rival”.\n\n2. So should I start updating my CV?\nlinking: “should‿I”\nchange: “updating” (t → d nhẹ)\nstrong: “CV”\n“should I” nối thành “shu-đai”. Giọng Úc cũng hay đọc t giữa hai nguyên âm thành d nhẹ: “ấp-đây-đing”. Từ viết tắt nhấn chữ cái cuối: C-V.\n\n3. Let's just say the walls in this building are very thin.\nchange: “just say” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “walls”, “very thin”\nCâu úp mở (ý là mình nghe lỏm được): “just say” mất t, đọc “jơs-sây”. Nhấn “very thin”, giọng tinh nghịch.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCụm bị động tường thuật (is said to, is thought to) đọc lướt, nhẹ; dồn trọng âm vào thông tin mới.\n“to have” sau động từ tường thuật đọc rất nhẹ: said to have → “set-tơ-hơv”.\nTừ viết tắt nhấn vào chữ cái cuối: C-E-O, C-V.\nGiọng Úc (Cora) thường không đọc r cuối từ, nhưng hay đọc t giữa hai nguyên âm thành d nhẹ như giọng Mỹ.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Allegedly.**\nNghe đồn là vậy (chưa ai xác nhận).\nTừ hay gặp trong tin tức. Đáp một từ này (thường nửa đùa) để tỏ ý mình chỉ nhắc lại lời đồn, không dám chắc.\nCách nói tương đương: So they say.\n\n**The ones who keep poaching our clients?**\nCái bên chuyên giành khách của mình ấy hả?\n“poach” khách hàng, nhân viên là lôi kéo, “câu” họ từ công ty khác về.\nCách nói tương đương: The ones who keep stealing our clients?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nIt is said / thought / believed that + mệnh đề\nBị động tường thuật: đưa tin mà không nêu nguồn, để giữ khoảng cách (chưa chắc là thật). Hay gặp trong tin tức, cuộc họp.\n[[It's said that]] the new boss is very strict.\n[[It's believed that]] the fire started in the kitchen.\n[[It's expected that]] prices will rise again.\n\nChủ ngữ + is said / thought / expected + to V / to have V3\nĐưa người hoặc vật lên làm chủ ngữ: to V cho hiện tại, tương lai; to have V3 cho việc đã xảy ra. Văn nói thân mật dùng be supposed to.\nThe singer [[is thought to be]] recovering at home.\nThe thief [[is believed to have left]] the country.\nThis café [[is supposed to be]] amazing.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Have you heard? Apparently we're being bought out!\nB: I've heard the rumors. The buyer is thought to be ________.\nA: Them? The ones who keep poaching our clients?\nB: Allegedly. And the deal is expected to be announced ________.\nA: Great. So should I start updating my CV?\nB: Not yet. Their CEO is said to have ________ last time.\nA: Last time? So they've done this before?\nB: Twice. They're supposed to be pretty decent employers, actually.\nA: Well, that's a relief. How do you know all this?\nB: Let's just say the walls in this building are very thin.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. The buyer is thought to be __our biggest rival__.\na. a tech company\nb. an overseas bank\nc. a private investor\n\n2. And the deal is expected to be announced __next month__.\na. any day now\nb. before Christmas\nc. by the end of the year\n\n3. Their CEO is said to have __kept everyone on__ last time.\na. cut half the staff\nb. doubled everyone's pay\nc. closed the old office\n",
