     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 5 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nEsther and Eddie are catching up over coffee.\nEsther: So, tell me everything. How's the new job?\nEddie: Really good, actually. Lots of travel.\nEsther: How glamorous. **Mind you**, I'd hate living out of a suitcase.\nEddie: It has its moments. Last week I got stuck in Chicago, and...\nEsther: Sorry, hang on. That's our coffee. Back in a sec.\nEddie: Thanks. **Anyway, as I was saying**, I slept at the airport.\nEsther: Poor you. Airports at night are the worst.\nEddie: Don't get me started. **Speaking of which**, did you ever book Japan?\nEsther: Finally, yes! Two weeks in April. I can't wait.\nEddie: Amazing! **Come to think of it**, my cousin's in Osaka. You could stay with her!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. Mind you, I'd hate living out of a suitcase.\nchange: “Mind‿you” (d + y → j)\nlinking: “out‿of‿a”\nstrong: “hate”, “suitcase”\n“Mind you” là một cụm riêng, đọc “main-ju” rồi ngắt nhẹ. Giọng Anh hay giữ t rõ khi nối: “out of a” → “ao-tơ-vơ”.\n\n2. Anyway, as I was saying, I slept at the airport.\nlinking: “as‿I”\nweak: “was”\nstrong: “Anyway”, “slept”, “airport”\n“Anyway” tách thành một nhịp, cuối hơi lên giọng để báo “mình kể tiếp đây”. “as I was saying” đọc nhanh, thấp: “ơ-zai-wơz-sây-ing”.\n\n3. Come to think of it, my cousin's in Osaka.\nweak: “to”\nlinking: “think‿of‿it”\nstrong: “cousin's”, “Osaka”\nCụm báo một ý vừa nảy ra: đọc nhanh, nhẹ; “think of it” nối thành “thin-kơ-vit”. Nhấn thông tin mới: “Osaka”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nDiscourse markers (Anyway, Mind you, Speaking of which) là một cụm riêng: đọc liền, rồi ngắt nhẹ trước ý chính.\n“Anyway” hơi lên giọng thường là mình nói tiếp; xuống giọng dứt khoát là muốn dừng chuyện.\n“Mind you” (nhưng mà) chủ yếu là lối nói Anh; người Mỹ hay nói “Then again”.\nGiọng Anh (Esther) giữ /j/ trong “new”: /njuː/; giọng Mỹ: /nuː/.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I'd hate living out of a suitcase.**\nMình thì chịu không nổi cảnh xách vali đi suốt.\n“live out of a suitcase” = đi suốt, chỗ nào cũng chỉ ở tạm vài hôm, đồ đạc lúc nào cũng nằm trong vali.\nCách nói tương đương: I'd hate always being on the road.\n\n**It has its moments.**\nLúc vui, lúc khổ ấy mà.\nÝ là không phải lúc nào cũng hay; ở đây Eddie thừa nhận đi công tác nhiều cũng có lúc vất vả.\nCách nói tương đương: It has its ups and downs.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nMind you / Speaking of which / Come to think of it\nMind you = nhưng mà (thêm ý ngược lại); Speaking of which = nhân nói đến chuyện đó; Come to think of it = giờ nghĩ lại mới nhớ ra.\nThe hotel was cheap. [[Mind you]], the beds were awful.\nI need a break. [[Speaking of which]], how was Bali?\n[[Come to think of it]], I haven't seen Sam all week.\n\nAnyway / As I was saying / Where was I?\nQuay lại câu chuyện chính sau khi bị ngắt hoặc lạc đề. “Anyway” còn dùng để đổi chủ đề hoặc kết thúc cuộc trò chuyện.\nSorry about that. [[As I was saying]], the plan is simple.\nNow, [[where was I]]? Oh yes, the budget.\n[[Anyway]], I'd better get going.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: So, tell me everything. How's the new job?\nB: Really good, actually. Lots of travel.\nA: How glamorous. Mind you, I'd hate living out of a suitcase.\nB: It has its moments. Last week I got stuck in Chicago, and...\nA: Sorry, hang on. That's our coffee. Back in a sec.\nB: Thanks. ________, I slept at the airport.\nA: Poor you. Airports at night are the worst.\nB: Don't get me started. ________, did you ever book Japan?\nA: Finally, yes! Two weeks in April. I can't wait.\nB: Amazing! ________, my cousin's in Osaka. You could stay with her!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. __Anyway, as I was saying__, I slept at the airport.\na. So, like I was saying\nb. Anyway, back to my story\nc. Where was I? Oh, right\n\n2. __Speaking of which__, did you ever book Japan?\na. Oh, that reminds me\nb. Speaking of travel\nc. On that note\n\n3. __Come to think of it__, my cousin's in Osaka.\na. Actually\nb. Now that I think about it\nc. Oh, by the way\n",
