     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 6 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nFlora fills Frederick in on a party he missed.\nFrederick: How was Jess's party, then? I'm gutted I missed it.\nFlora: So much fun. There were, like, fifty people **or something**.\nFrederick: Fifty? In that tiny flat? Where did everyone stand?\nFlora: Everywhere! It was **sort of** chaotic, but in a good way.\nFrederick: Was it a proper party? Dancing **and all that**?\nFlora: Not really. Snacks, board games **and stuff**. Then **a bunch of** us did karaoke.\nFrederick: Oh no. Please tell me you didn't sing.\nFlora: Just one song! But we didn't leave till **two-ish**.\nFrederick: Two-ish? On a school night? I'm impressed.\nFlora: Don't be. I'm **kind of** paying for it today.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. There were, like, fifty people or something.\nweak: “like”, “or something”\nstrong: “fifty”\n“like” là từ đệm, chen vào nhanh và nhẹ. “or something” đọc lướt, thấp giọng: “ơ-sơm-thing”. Nhấn mạnh nhất vào con số “fifty”.\n\n2. It was sort of chaotic, but in a good way.\nchange: “sort of” (→ “sorta”)\nlinking: “but‿in‿a”\nstrong: “chaotic”, “good way”\nNói nhanh, “sort of” thành “sorta” /ˈsɔːrɾə/ “sor-đơ”. Giọng Mỹ: “but in a” nối, t thành d nhẹ: “bơ-đi-nơ”.\n\n3. How was Jess's party, then?\nweak: “was”, “then”\nstrong: “Jess's party”\n“Jess's” thêm một âm tiết /ˈdʒesɪz/: “je-siz”. Giọng Anh: “party” /ˈpɑːti/, không có r, t rõ (giọng Mỹ: “par-đi”). “then” cuối câu đọc nhẹ, thấp.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nTừ ngữ mơ hồ (sort of, kind of, or something, and stuff) đọc nhẹ, nhanh, thấp giọng; dồn nhấn vào từ chính.\nNói nhanh: sort of → “sorta”, kind of → “kinda”, a bunch of → “ơ-bơn-chơ”.\n“-ish” gắn sau số hoặc tính từ: two-ish = khoảng hai giờ; nhấn vào số: TWO-ish.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I'm gutted I missed it.**\nTiếc đứt ruột vì lỡ mất.\n“gutted” là từ lóng của người Anh: rất buồn, thất vọng.\nCách nói tương đương: I'm so sad I missed it.\n\n**I'm kind of paying for it today.**\nHôm nay mình đang lãnh đủ đây.\n“pay for it” = lãnh hậu quả (mệt, đau đầu…) vì việc đã làm hôm trước.\nCách nói tương đương: I'm really feeling it today.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nsort of / kind of: nói giảm cho mềm\nĐặt trước tính từ hoặc động từ để nói mơ hồ, bớt khẳng định. Chủ yếu dùng trong văn nói thân mật.\nThe film was [[kind of]] boring, to be honest.\nI [[sort of]] forgot to call her back.\n\nor something / and stuff / a bunch of / -ish\n“or something”, “and stuff” thêm vào cuối câu, cuối danh sách khi không cần nói chính xác; “a bunch of” = một đống, nhiều; “-ish” gắn sau giờ, tuổi, tính từ: seven-ish, forty-ish.\nLet's meet at [[seven-ish]].\nWe bought [[a bunch of]] snacks, drinks [[and stuff]].\nHe's a dentist [[or something]].\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: How was Jess's party, then? I'm gutted I missed it.\nB: So much fun. There were, like, fifty people or something.\nA: Fifty? In that tiny flat? Where did everyone stand?\nB: Everywhere! It was ________ chaotic, but in a good way.\nA: Was it a proper party? Dancing and all that?\nB: Not really. Snacks, board games ________. Then a bunch of us did karaoke.\nA: Oh no. Please tell me you didn't sing.\nB: Just one song! But we didn't leave till ________.\nA: Two-ish? On a school night? I'm impressed.\nB: Don't be. I'm kind of paying for it today.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. It was __sort of__ chaotic, but in a good way.\na. kind of\nb. a bit\nc. pretty\n\n2. Snacks, board games __and stuff__.\na. and things like that\nb. and whatnot\nc. and so on\n\n3. But we didn't leave till __two-ish__.\na. one thirty or so\nb. nearly three\nc. way past midnight\n",
