     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 8 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nGraham is trying to talk Gemma into running a half marathon.\nGraham: Gemma. The city half marathon in March. You and me. What do you reckon?\nGemma: You're kidding, right? I get winded climbing stairs.\nGraham: That's what training's for. **Just imagine** crossing that finish line.\nGemma: I'd rather imagine brunch. Seriously, what if I can't finish?\nGraham: **What's the worst that could happen?** You walk a bit. Heaps of people do.\nGemma: **I'm still not convinced.** Three months of early mornings?\nGraham: **Tell you what**, I'll run every session with you. Rain, hail or shine.\nGemma: Even the crack-of-dawn ones?\nGraham: Especially those. Come on, **you've got nothing to lose**.\nGemma: Fine, **you've talked me into it**. But the coffee's on you.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. What's the worst that could happen?\nstrong: “worst”, “happen”\nweak: “that could”\nCâu trấn an: giọng thoải mái, xuống ở cuối. “that could” đọc lướt: “đơt-kơd”. Giọng Úc thường không đọc r: “worst” /wɜːst/.\n\n2. I'd rather imagine brunch.\nlinking: “rather‿imagine”\nstrong: “brunch”\nCâu đùa: nhấn mạnh “brunch” để đối lập với “finish line” của Graham. Giọng Mỹ đọc rõ r và nối sang từ sau: “ra-đơ-ri-ma-jin”.\n\n3. Fine, you've talked me into it.\nstrong: “Fine”, “talked”\nlinking: “into‿it”\n“Fine” kéo dài, hạ giọng: đồng ý nhưng miễn cưỡng. Chữ l trong “talked” câm: /tɔːkt/. “into it” nối bằng âm w nhẹ: “in-tu-wit”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nThuyết phục: giọng nhiệt tình, nhấn vào từ gợi hình ảnh (imagine, finish line, nothing to lose).\nĐồng ý miễn cưỡng (Fine…, OK…): kéo dài và hạ giọng.\nChữ l câm trong talk, walk, could, would, should.\nGiọng Úc (Graham) thường đọc “half” là /hɑːf/ như giọng Anh; giọng Mỹ (Gemma) đọc /hæf/.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Rain, hail or shine.**\nDù mưa hay nắng.\nCách nói của người Úc (người Mỹ, Anh hay nói “rain or shine”): việc gì cũng làm, bất kể thời tiết.\nCách nói tương đương: Whatever the weather.\n\n**Even the crack-of-dawn ones?**\nCả mấy buổi chạy lúc tờ mờ sáng á?\n“at the crack of dawn” = lúc tờ mờ sáng, rất sớm; ở đây gạch nối thành tính từ: crack-of-dawn runs.\nCách nói tương đương: Even the really early ones?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nThuyết phục người khác\nGợi ra hình ảnh tích cực, xoá bớt nỗi lo, rồi đưa thêm một lời đề nghị hấp dẫn. Giọng nhiệt tình nhưng đừng ép.\n[[Just imagine]] how good you'll feel afterwards.\nCome on, [[what have you got to lose]]?\n[[Tell you what]], I'll pay for the tickets.\n\nĐáp lại lời thuyết phục\nChưa đồng ý: I'm not convinced / not sold. Đã đồng ý: You've talked me into it / You've won me over. Kèm điều kiện: On one condition.\nI'm [[not sold]] on the idea yet.\nOK, [[you've won me over]].\nI'll come, [[on one condition]].\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: Gemma. The city half marathon in March. You and me. What do you reckon?\nB: You're kidding, right? I get winded climbing stairs.\nA: That's what training's for. Just imagine crossing that finish line.\nB: I'd rather imagine brunch. Seriously, what if I ________?\nA: What's the worst that could happen? You walk a bit. Heaps of people do.\nB: I'm still not ________. Three months of early mornings?\nA: Tell you what, I'll run every session with you. Rain, hail or shine.\nB: Even the crack-of-dawn ones?\nA: Especially those. Come on, you've got nothing to lose.\nB: Fine, you've ________. But the coffee's on you.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. Seriously, what if I __can't finish__?\na. get injured\nb. come last\nc. give up halfway\n\n2. I'm still not __convinced__.\na. sold on it\nb. sure about this\nc. on board\n\n3. Fine, you've __talked me into it__.\na. won me over\nb. convinced me\nc. worn me down\n",
