     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 9 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nVu has a job offer in Melbourne and asks Harriet for advice.\nHarriet: So, have you **made a decision** about Melbourne yet?\nVu: Not yet. I keep **having second thoughts**.\nHarriet: About the job itself, or the move?\nVu: The move. I don't want to **make a huge mistake**.\nHarriet: I get that. But have you **done the maths** on the salary?\nVu: I **did the math** last night. Financially, it **makes sense**.\nHarriet: Then it's a no-brainer! Sometimes you've just got to **take the plunge**.\nVu: You would say that. You grew up there.\nHarriet: True. So **have a chat** with my brother. He'll show you the ropes.\nVu: That'd help a lot. OK, I'll take it before I change my mind.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. Not yet. I keep having second thoughts.\nchange: “Not‿yet” (t + y → ch)\nstrong: “second thoughts”\n“Not yet” nối thành “na-chét”. Âm d của “second” gần như mất trước “thoughts”: “se-cơn-thots”.\n\n2. Sometimes you've just got to take the plunge.\nchange: “got to” (→ “gotta”)\nweak: “you've”\nstrong: “Sometimes”, “plunge”\nNói nhanh, “got to” thành “gotta” /ˈɡɒɾə/, “just” mất t: “jơs”. Giọng Úc cũng hay đọc t giữa hai nguyên âm thành d nhẹ.\n\n3. You would say that.\nweak: “You”\nstrong: “would”\nTrêu nhẹ: nhấn mạnh “would”, đọc đủ /wʊd/ (không rút thành 'd), ý là “bạn thì tất nhiên nói vậy rồi”. “say that” hạ giọng.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nCollocation (make a decision, take the plunge) đọc liền như một khối, nhấn vào danh từ.\nNói nhanh: got to → “gotta”, want to → “wanna”, going to → “gonna”, don't know → “dunno”.\nt + y nối thành “ch”: not yet → “na-chét”, got you → “ga-chu”.\nNhấn trợ động từ để tỏ ý “biết ngay mà”: You WOULD say that.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Then it's a no-brainer!**\nVậy thì còn phải nghĩ gì nữa!\n“a no-brainer” là quyết định dễ đến mức không cần suy nghĩ.\nCách nói tương đương: Then it's an easy decision.\n\n**He'll show you the ropes.**\nAnh ấy sẽ chỉ cho bạn đường đi nước bước.\n“show someone the ropes” = hướng dẫn người mới cách làm, cách xoay xở ở nơi mới.\nCách nói tương đương: He'll help you get started.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nmake và do\nmake: tạo ra, đưa ra (a decision, a mistake, sense). do: thực hiện một việc (research, homework, a favor). Anh, Úc nói do the maths; Mỹ nói do the math.\nI [[made a mistake]] on the form.\nCould you [[do me a favor]]?\nWe [[did some research]] before buying the car.\n\ntake và have\ntake: chấp nhận, nắm lấy (a risk, a chance, your time, the plunge). have: trải qua, có (second thoughts, a chat, a go, a look).\n[[Take your time]], there's no rush.\nShe [[took a big risk]] starting her own business.\nCan I [[have a go]]?\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: So, have you made a decision about Melbourne yet?\nB: Not yet. I keep ________.\nA: About the job itself, or the move?\nB: The move. I don't want to ________.\nA: I get that. But have you done the maths on the salary?\nB: I did the math last night. Financially, it makes sense.\nA: Then it's a no-brainer! Sometimes you've just got to take the plunge.\nB: You would say that. You grew up there.\nA: True. So have a chat with my brother. He'll show you the ropes.\nB: That'd help a lot. OK, I'll take it before I ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. I keep __having second thoughts__.\na. changing my mind\nb. going back and forth\nc. putting it off\n\n2. I don't want to __make a huge mistake__.\na. make the wrong call\nb. take that risk\nc. do anything rash\n\n3. OK, I'll take it before I __change my mind__.\na. lose my nerve\nb. get cold feet\nc. talk myself out of it\n",
