     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 10 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nIt's day five of non-stop rain on Hamish and Imogen's beach trip.\nHamish: Well, it's looking **a bit damp** out there again.\nImogen: A bit damp? The street's basically a river, Hamish!\nHamish: **Not ideal**, I'll admit. But at least the garden's getting a good drink.\nImogen: **Oh, great.** That makes me feel so much better.\nHamish: Look on the bright side. We've finished three jigsaw puzzles.\nImogen: **Living the dream.** I packed four swimsuits for this trip.\nHamish: You could always wear one in the bath.\nImogen: **Very funny.** So is it going to clear up tomorrow?\nHamish: Glorious sunshine, apparently. Though they said that yesterday, too.\nImogen: **Oh, wonderful.** I'll believe it when I see it.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. Not ideal, I'll admit.\nstrong: “Not ideal”\nlinking: “I'll‿admit”\nNói giảm kiểu Anh: giọng đều, bình thản như không có gì, dù tình huống khá tệ. “I'll admit” nối thành “ai-lơd-mít”.\n\n2. Oh, great. That makes me feel so much better.\nstrong: “great”, “so much better”\nMỉa mai: “great” đọc thấp, phẳng, kéo dài; “so much better” nhấn quá mức. Nghĩa thật là ngược lại: chẳng thấy khá hơn chút nào.\n\n3. You could always wear one in the bath.\nweak: “could”\nlinking: “one‿in‿the”\nstrong: “always”, “bath”\nCâu đùa tỉnh bơ: giọng đều, nhấn “always” và “bath”. Giọng Anh chuẩn đọc “bath” /bɑːθ/ (a dài), giọng Mỹ đọc /bæθ/.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nMỉa mai: từ tích cực (great, wonderful) đọc thấp, phẳng, kéo dài; người nghe hiểu nghĩa ngược lại.\nCùng là “Oh, great!”: lên giọng, tươi tắn là khen thật; phẳng, kéo dài là mỉa.\nNói giảm kiểu Anh (a bit damp, not ideal): giọng bình thản, càng tỉnh càng buồn cười.\nNói nhanh, “going to” thành “gonna” (“gơ-nơ”): is it gonna clear up?\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Look on the bright side.**\nNhìn vào mặt tích cực đi.\nDùng để an ủi, hoặc nói đùa khi tình huống chẳng có gì tích cực.\nCách nói tương đương: At least it's not all bad.\n\n**I'll believe it when I see it.**\nThấy tận mắt mới tin.\nTỏ ý nghi ngờ một lời hứa hay một dự báo.\nCách nói tương đương: I'm not holding my breath.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nNói giảm (understatement)\nNói nhẹ đi một tình huống tệ để hài hước hoặc giữ bình tĩnh, rất phổ biến ở người Anh: a bit, not ideal, not the best, could be better.\nLosing your passport abroad is [[not ideal]].\nMy first day was [[not the best]], to be honest.\nThat presentation [[could have gone better]].\n\nMỉa mai (sarcasm)\nDùng từ tích cực với ngữ điệu phẳng, kéo dài để nói điều ngược lại. Hay gặp: Great. / Lovely. / Just what I needed. / Yeah, right.\nA flat tire? [[Great]]. [[Just what I needed]].\nHe'll be on time? [[Yeah, right]].\nOh, [[brilliant]]. The printer's broken again.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Well, it's looking a bit damp out there again.\nB: A bit damp? The street's basically ________, Hamish!\nA: Not ideal, I'll admit. But at least the garden's getting a good drink.\nB: Oh, great. That makes me feel so much better.\nA: Look on the bright side. We've finished three jigsaw puzzles.\nB: ________. I packed four swimsuits for this trip.\nA: You could always wear one in the bath.\nB: Very funny. So is it going to clear up tomorrow?\nA: Glorious sunshine, apparently. Though they said that yesterday, too.\nB: ________. I'll believe it when I see it.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. The street's basically __a river__, Hamish!\na. a swimming pool\nb. a lake\nc. underwater\n\n2. __Living the dream__. I packed four swimsuits for this trip.\na. Best vacation ever\nb. This is the life\nc. Just my luck\n\n3. __Oh, wonderful__. I'll believe it when I see it.\na. Yeah, right\nb. Oh, sure\nc. Fat chance\n",
