     "md": "Level 9/unit 11/unit 11.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 11 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nThu and Kieran are waiting for their exam results to go online at noon.\nThu: It's twelve o'clock. Why isn't the results page loading yet?\nKieran: Everyone's refreshing at once. I've been **on edge** all morning.\nThu: Same here. I've had **butterflies in my stomach** since breakfast.\nKieran: Seriously, I'm **fed up with** this website. It crashed last year, too.\nThu: Wait, it's working! Oh my goodness, I actually passed!\nKieran: Way to go! I knew you would. OK, my turn.\nThu: Well? Don't leave me hanging!\nKieran: I passed, too! What **a weight off my shoulders**.\nThu: I'm **over the moon**. I could cry, honestly.\nKieran: Don't, or you'll set me off. Let's go celebrate instead.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. I've been on edge all morning.\nlinking: “on‿edge‿all”\nstrong: “edge”, “morning”\n“on edge all” nối liền thành “a-ne-jol”. Giọng Mỹ đọc rõ r trong “morning”: /ˈmɔːrnɪŋ/.\n\n2. Well? Don't leave me hanging!\nchange: “Don't leave” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “Well”, “hanging”\n“Well?” lên giọng, sốt ruột chờ câu trả lời. Âm t của “Don't” mất trước “leave”: “đâun-li:v”.\n\n3. What a weight off my shoulders.\nlinking: “What‿a”, “weight‿off”\nstrong: “weight”, “shoulders”\nGiọng Mỹ: t giữa hai nguyên âm thành d nhẹ, “What a” → “wa-đơ”, “weight off” → “wei-đóf”. Câu cảm thán xuống giọng ở cuối.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nThành ngữ cảm xúc: nhấn vào từ hình ảnh (EDGE, MOON, WEIGHT), đọc nhẹ giới từ và mạo từ.\nCâu cảm thán What a…! xuống giọng mạnh ở cuối.\nGiọng Anh (Thu): don't, so, go đọc /əʊ/ “âu”; giọng Mỹ (Kieran) đọc /oʊ/ “ôu”.\nCâu hỏi một từ (Well?) lên giọng để giục người kia nói tiếp.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Don't leave me hanging!**\nĐừng bắt mình chờ nữa!\nGiục người kia nói ngay kết quả hoặc câu trả lời.\nCách nói tương đương: Don't keep me in suspense!\n\n**Don't, or you'll set me off.**\nĐừng mà, không mình khóc theo bây giờ.\n“set someone off” = làm ai bắt đầu khóc (hoặc cười) theo.\nCách nói tương đương: Stop, or I'll start crying too.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nThành ngữ chỉ lo lắng, bực bội\non edge, a bundle of nerves (bồn chồn, lo lắng); butterflies in my stomach (hồi hộp); fed up with (chán ngấy, bực mình vì).\nShe's been [[on edge]] since the interview.\nI always get [[butterflies]] before a big match.\nI'm [[fed up with]] all this rain.\n\nThành ngữ chỉ vui mừng, nhẹ nhõm\nover the moon, on cloud nine (vui sướng tột độ); a weight off my shoulders (trút được gánh nặng).\nShe was [[over the moon]] about the baby.\nPaying off the loan was [[a weight off my shoulders]].\nHe's been [[on cloud nine]] since the wedding.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: It's twelve o'clock. Why isn't the results page loading yet?\nB: Everyone's refreshing at once. I've been ________ all morning.\nA: Same here. I've had butterflies in my stomach since breakfast.\nB: Seriously, I'm ________ this website. It crashed last year, too.\nA: Wait, it's working! Oh my goodness, I actually passed!\nB: Way to go! I knew you would. OK, my turn.\nA: Well? Don't leave me hanging!\nB: I passed, too! What ________.\nA: I'm over the moon. I could cry, honestly.\nB: Don't, or you'll set me off. Let's go celebrate instead.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. I've been __on edge__ all morning.\na. a nervous wreck\nb. a bundle of nerves\nc. climbing the walls\n\n2. Seriously, I'm __fed up with__ this website.\na. sick and tired of\nb. so done with\nc. losing my patience with\n\n3. What __a weight off my shoulders__.\na. a relief\nb. a load off my mind\nc. a dream come true\n",
