     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 12 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nLorna has a funny story to tell Rupert about last night.\nRupert: Come on, you've been giggling all morning. What's the story?\nLorna: **You'll never guess** what I did at the conference dinner last night.\nRupert: Go on. Did you fall asleep during a speech?\nLorna: Worse. **So there I am**, asking this guy in a suit for more bread.\nRupert: As you do.\nLorna: Well, I thought he was a waiter! Then, **get this**, they call him up on stage.\nRupert: Oh no. Don't tell me he was the keynote speaker.\nLorna: Yep. And he started his talk with a joke about it.\nRupert: He didn't! What did you do?\nLorna: **Long story short**, I'm never asking anyone for bread again.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. Then, get this, they call him up on stage.\nstrong: “get this”, “stage”\nlinking: “call‿him‿up”\n“get this” (nghe này) tách riêng, ngắt trước và sau để tạo hồi hộp. “him” mất h, nối thành “ca-li-mấp”.\n\n2. Don't tell me he was the keynote speaker.\nlinking: “Don't‿tell”\nstrong: “keynote speaker”\nĐoán trước điều tệ, giọng lo lắng. Hai âm t gộp làm một: “đâun-tel”. Giọng Anh thường không đọc r cuối: /ˈspiːkə/.\n\n3. Long story short, I'm never asking anyone for bread again.\nstrong: “never”, “bread”\nweak: “for”\nNgắt sau “Long story short”, rồi nói chậm lại ở câu chốt; nhấn “never” và “bread” để gây cười.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\n“So there I am…” đọc chậm, hơi kéo dài “So”, rồi ngắt nhẹ để người nghe hình dung cảnh.\n“You'll never guess…”, “get this” báo hiệu chuyện bất ngờ: nói chậm, rõ, ngắt sau đó.\nCâu chốt (punchline) nói chậm, xuống giọng, rồi dừng để người nghe cười.\nĐại từ him, her, his đọc nhẹ thường mất h: call him up → “ca-li-mấp”.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**As you do.**\nChuyện thường ngày ấy mà (nói đùa).\nCâu đùa tỉnh bơ của người Anh: giả vờ coi một việc kỳ quặc là chuyện hết sức bình thường.\nCách nói tương đương: As one does.\n\n**He didn't!**\nKhông thể nào!\nĐáp bằng trợ động từ ở thể phủ định, xuống giọng mạnh, để tỏ ý không tin nổi (nửa sốc, nửa buồn cười).\nCách nói tương đương: No way!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nMở đầu và dựng cảnh: You'll never guess… / So there I am…\nBáo hiệu sắp kể chuyện bất ngờ, rồi dùng thì hiện tại để đưa người nghe vào cảnh như đang xảy ra.\n[[You'll never guess]] who I bumped into today.\n[[So there I am]], standing in the rain with no keys.\n[[And get this]], the car wasn't even ours.\n\nKết chuyện: Long story short… / Anyway, the point is…\nRút gọn phần dài dòng để đi thẳng đến kết quả hoặc câu chốt. Người Anh hay nói To cut a long story short.\n[[Long story short]], we missed the flight.\n[[To cut a long story short]], they got married.\n[[Anyway, the point is]], always check the date.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: Come on, you've been giggling all morning. What's the story?\nB: You'll never guess ________ at the conference dinner last night.\nA: Go on. Did you fall asleep during a speech?\nB: Worse. So there I am, asking this guy in a suit for ________.\nA: As you do.\nB: Well, I thought he was a waiter! Then, get this, they call him up on stage.\nA: Oh no. Don't tell me he was the keynote speaker.\nB: Yep. And he started his talk with a joke about it.\nA: He didn't! What did you do?\nB: ________, I'm never asking anyone for bread again.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. You'll never guess __what I did__ at the conference dinner last night.\na. who I met\nb. what happened\nc. who I sat next to\n\n2. So there I am, asking this guy in a suit for __more bread__.\na. a glass of water\nb. the dessert menu\nc. another coffee\n\n3. __Long story short__, I'm never asking anyone for bread again.\na. To cut a long story short\nb. Needless to say\nc. Anyway\n",
