     "md": "Level 10/unit 1/unit 1.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 1 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nAnnabel and Alistair share a flat in London. Annabel wants to talk about the chores.\nAnnabel: Alistair, have you got a minute? It's about the kitchen.\nAlistair: Uh-oh. That sounds serious. Is it the washing-up again?\nAnnabel: Well, yes. It's **high time** we **sorted** out a proper rota, don't you think?\nAlistair: Fair enough. But **I'd rather** we **didn't** make it too strict.\nAnnabel: Fine by me. **I'd just rather** you **didn't** leave pans soaking for three days.\nAlistair: Guilty as charged. They do tend to pile up, I'll admit.\nAnnabel: So how about you handle the washing-up, and I'll take the bins out?\nAlistair: Deal. And **it's about time** we **bought** a dishwasher, frankly.\nAnnabel: Now you're talking! I'll look into it this weekend.\nAlistair: Brilliant. Consider the rota officially up and running!\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. It's high time we sorted out a proper rota, don't you think?\nlinking: “sorted‿out”\nchange: “don't‿you” (t + y → “ch”)\nweak: “we”, “a”\nstrong: “high time”, “proper rota”\nGiọng Ireland đọc rõ /r/: “sorted out” → “sor-tị-đao”. “don't you” đọc thành “đôn-chu”. Câu hỏi đuôi xuống giọng vì người nói mong được đồng ý.\n\n2. I'd just rather you didn't leave pans soaking for three days.\nchange: “just rather” (mất âm t)\nstrong: “didn't”, “pans”, “three days”\n“just rather” đọc thành “jơs-ra-đơr”. Nhấn “didn't” để nói rõ điều mình không muốn, nhưng giữ giọng nhẹ nhàng để lời phàn nàn vẫn lịch sự.\n\n3. Guilty as charged.\nlinking: “Guilty‿as”\nstrong: “Guilty”, “charged”\nChữ “u” trong “guilty” câm: /ˈɡɪlti/. “charged” chỉ có một âm tiết, đuôi -ed đọc /d/: “cha:jd”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nGiọng Ireland (Annabel) đọc rõ /r/ sau nguyên âm (sorted, proper); giọng Anh (Alistair) thì không: charged → “cha:jd”.\nKhi phàn nàn lịch sự, nhấn vào từ mang ý chính (didn't, high time) nhưng giữ giọng mềm.\nÂm /t/ đứng trước “you” biến thành “ch”: don't you → “đôn-chu”.\nCâu hỏi đuôi xuống giọng khi người nói chờ sự đồng tình, lên giọng khi thật sự muốn hỏi.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Guilty as charged.**\nỪ, lỗi của tôi, tôi nhận.\nThành ngữ vui (gốc là lời tuyên có tội ở toà) để thừa nhận mình sai một cách hài hước.\nCách nói tương đương: I hold my hands up.\n\n**Now you're talking!**\nThế mới phải chứ!\nDùng khi người kia đưa ra một đề xuất mà mình rất thích.\nCách nói tương đương: That's more like it!\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nIt's (high / about) time + chủ ngữ + quá khứ đơn\nNói việc lẽ ra phải làm từ lâu rồi. Động từ chia quá khứ nhưng nghĩa là hiện tại; “high time” mạnh hơn “about time”.\nIt's [[high time]] you [[got]] a proper job.\n[[It's about time]] they [[fixed]] that road.\n\nwould rather + chủ ngữ + quá khứ đơn\nCách lịch sự, gián tiếp để nói mình muốn người khác làm hoặc đừng làm gì. Nói về chính mình thì dùng would rather + động từ nguyên mẫu.\n[[I'd rather]] you [[didn't]] smoke in here.\n[[I'd rather stay]] in tonight, if you don't mind.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: Alistair, have you got a minute? It's about the kitchen.\nB: Uh-oh. That sounds serious. Is it the washing-up again?\nA: Well, yes. It's high time we sorted out a proper rota, don't you think?\nB: Fair enough. But I'd rather we didn't ________.\nA: Fine by me. I'd just rather you didn't leave pans soaking for three days.\nB: Guilty as charged. They do tend to ________, I'll admit.\nA: So how about you handle the washing-up, and I'll take the bins out?\nB: Deal. And it's about time we ________, frankly.\nA: Now you're talking! I'll look into it this weekend.\nB: Brilliant. Consider the rota officially up and running!\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. But I'd rather we didn't __make it too strict__.\na. turn it into a big deal\nb. make it too complicated\nc. argue about it\n\n2. They do tend to __pile up__, I'll admit.\na. get forgotten\nb. slip my mind\nc. sit there for ages\n\n3. And it's about time we __bought a dishwasher__, frankly.\na. hired a cleaner\nb. got a bigger sink\nc. replaced that old kettle\n",
