     "md": "Level 10/unit 2/unit 2.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 2 — CD1\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nBenedict and Celeste are getting married at a vineyard on Saturday. The nerves are kicking in.\nBenedict: Bad news. It's **supposed to** bucket down on Saturday.\nCeleste: Figures. Well, something was **bound to** go wrong. At least we've got the tent.\nBenedict: True. And I've finished all the place cards. By hand.\nCeleste: Oh, babe. Didn't I tell you? The venue prints them for free.\nBenedict: You're kidding. So I **needn't have** stayed up till two?\nCeleste: Oops, my bad. Hey, aren't you **supposed to** be writing your speech?\nBenedict: Working on it. Your mum's **bound to** cry, whatever I say.\nCeleste: She cries at commercials, so that's a given. Just keep it under five minutes.\nBenedict: Five minutes? You're **supposed to** be on my side!\nCeleste: I am. That's why I'm giving you a time limit.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. You're kidding. So I needn't have stayed up till two?\nchange: “kidding” (i → ơ)\nlinking: “needn't‿have”, “stayed‿up”\nstrong: “kidding”, “needn't”, “two”\nGiọng New Zealand thường đọc /ɪ/ gần như “ơ”: “cơ-đing”. “have” đọc yếu /əv/, mất /h/: “ní-đơn-tơv”. Lên giọng ở cuối vì bất ngờ.\n\n2. Well, something was bound to go wrong.\nchange: “bound to” (mất âm d)\nweak: “was”, “to”\nstrong: “bound”, “wrong”\n“bound to” đọc thành “bao-ntơ”. Chữ w trong “wrong” câm: /rɔːŋ/. Xuống giọng ở cuối, kiểu chán nản: biết ngay mà.\n\n3. Hey, aren't you supposed to be writing your speech?\nchange: “aren't‿you” (t + y → “ch”)\nweak: “to”, “your”\nstrong: “supposed”, “speech”\n“supposed to” đọc liền, mất /d/: “sơ-pâus-tơ”. Giọng Mỹ: “writing” → “rai-đing”. Câu hỏi phủ định để nhắc khéo nên xuống giọng.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nKhi nói nhanh, /d/ giữa hai phụ âm thường mất: supposed to → “sơ-pâus-tơ”, bound to → “bao-ntơ”.\n“have” sau needn't, should, could đọc yếu /əv/: needn't have → “ní-đơn-tơv”.\nGiọng New Zealand thường đọc /ɪ/ gần “ơ” (kidding, fish); giọng Mỹ đọc t giữa hai nguyên âm thành “d” nhẹ.\nNhấn mạnh từ mang cảm xúc (needn't, two) để lộ vẻ tiếc công, ngạc nhiên.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**It's supposed to bucket down on Saturday.**\nNghe nói thứ Bảy trời sẽ mưa như trút nước.\n“bucket down” (Anh, Úc, New Zealand) = mưa rất to. “be supposed to” ở đây nghĩa là “nghe nói, theo dự báo”.\nCách nói tương đương: It's meant to pour on Saturday.\n\n**She cries at commercials, so that's a given.**\nMẹ em xem quảng cáo còn khóc, nên chuyện đó khỏi phải bàn.\n“that's a given” = điều hiển nhiên. “commercials” là từ Mỹ; người Anh hay nói “adverts”.\nCách nói tương đương: That goes without saying.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nbe bound to / be supposed to + động từ nguyên mẫu\nbound to: chắc chắn sẽ xảy ra. supposed to: lẽ ra phải (theo kế hoạch, quy định, vai trò), hoặc “nghe nói là”.\nDon't worry, they're [[bound to]] love you.\nThe bus [[was supposed to]] come at nine.\nThis film [[is supposed to]] be brilliant.\n\nneedn't have + V3 / didn't need to + V\nneedn't have: đã làm nhưng hoá ra không cần (tiếc công). didn't need to: không cần làm, thường là đã không làm. Người Mỹ ít dùng needn't.\nYou [[needn't have brought]] wine. We've got plenty.\nI [[didn't need to]] queue, so I walked straight in.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Bad news. It's supposed to bucket down on Saturday.\nB: Figures. Well, something was bound to ________. At least we've got the tent.\nA: True. And I've finished all the place cards. By hand.\nB: Oh, babe. Didn't I tell you? The venue prints them for free.\nA: You're kidding. So I needn't have stayed up till two?\nB: Oops, my bad. Hey, aren't you supposed to be ________?\nA: Working on it. Your mum's bound to cry, whatever I say.\nB: She cries at commercials, so that's a given. Just keep it ________.\nA: Five minutes? You're supposed to be on my side!\nB: I am. That's why I'm giving you a time limit.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. Well, something was bound to __go wrong__.\na. come up\nb. go sideways\nc. slip through the cracks\n\n2. Hey, aren't you supposed to be __writing your speech__?\na. picking up your suit\nb. calling the band\nc. finishing the seating chart\n\n3. Just keep it __under five minutes__.\na. short and sweet\nb. clean\nc. light and funny\n",
