     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 5 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nFelicity has asked Elias, one of her team, for a quick word.\nFelicity: Thanks for staying back, Elias. **I wanted to flag** something from today's meeting.\nElias: Sure. Is everything okay?\nFelicity: Mostly. But **I've noticed** you tend to jump in before others finish.\nElias: Oh. I didn't realize I was doing that.\nFelicity: It comes from a good place, I know. But the juniors have gone a bit quiet.\nElias: That's fair. **I appreciate you** being upfront about it.\nFelicity: **It might be worth** letting others finish first, then building on their ideas.\nElias: Makes sense. I guess I get excited and forget to listen.\nFelicity: Totally get it. Your energy's a real asset, so don't lose that.\nElias: Thanks. Could you give me a nudge if I slip up?\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. I wanted to flag something from today's meeting.\nchange: “wanted to” (mất âm d)\nstrong: “flag”, “today's meeting”\nGiọng New Zealand thường đọc /æ/ gần như “e”: “flag” nghe như “fleg”. “wanted to” → “won-tị-tơ”. Nói chậm, giọng nhẹ để lời góp ý không nặng nề.\n\n2. That's fair. I appreciate you being upfront about it.\nchange: “appreciate‿you” (t + y → “ch”)\nlinking: “upfront‿about‿it”\nstrong: “fair”, “upfront”\n“appreciate you” → “ơ-pri-shi-ây-chu”. Giọng Mỹ: “about it” → “ơ-bao-đit”. Xuống giọng ở cuối để nghe chân thành, không phòng thủ.\n\n3. Could you give me a nudge if I slip up?\nchange: “Could‿you” (d + y → “j”)\nlinking: “slip‿up”\nweak: “me”, “a”\nstrong: “nudge”, “slip up”\n“Could you” → “cu-ju”; “give me” nói nhanh gần như “gim-mi”. Lên giọng nhẹ ở cuối: lời nhờ vả lịch sự.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nGiọng New Zealand thường đọc /æ/ gần “e” (flag, back), /ɪ/ gần “ơ” (finish).\nÂm d, t gặp “you” biến thành “j”, “ch”: could you → “cu-ju”, appreciate you → “…ây-chu”.\nKhi góp ý, nói chậm và giọng đều; khi nhận góp ý, xuống giọng ở cuối câu để nghe thành thật.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**It comes from a good place, I know.**\nChị biết em có ý tốt mà.\n“come from a good place” = xuất phát từ ý tốt. Câu làm mềm trước khi nói điều khó nghe.\nCách nói tương đương: I know you mean well.\n\n**Could you give me a nudge if I slip up?**\nNếu em lại mắc lỗi thì chị nhắc khéo em nhé?\n“give someone a nudge” = nhắc khéo (nghĩa đen: huých nhẹ); “slip up” = sơ suất.\nCách nói tương đương: Feel free to remind me if I do it again.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nGóp ý khéo: I wanted to flag… / I've noticed… / It might be worth + V-ing\nMở lời nhẹ nhàng, nói về hành động cụ thể (không chê con người), rồi gợi ý thay vì ra lệnh.\n[[I wanted to flag]] a small issue with the slides.\n[[I've noticed]] you've been quiet in meetings lately.\n[[It might be worth]] double-checking the figures.\n\nĐón nhận góp ý: I appreciate you + V-ing / That's fair\nCảm ơn và thừa nhận một cách chuyên nghiệp, không phòng thủ. Có thể nói appreciate + you + V-ing hoặc appreciate + danh từ (your honesty).\n[[I appreciate you telling]] me.\n[[That's fair]]. I'll work on it.\n[[Point taken]]. It won't happen again.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: Thanks for staying back, Elias. I wanted to flag something from today's meeting.\nB: Sure. Is everything okay?\nA: Mostly. But I've noticed you tend to jump in before others finish.\nB: Oh. I didn't realize ________.\nA: It comes from a good place, I know. But the juniors have gone a bit quiet.\nB: That's fair. I appreciate you ________.\nA: It might be worth letting others finish first, then building on their ideas.\nB: Makes sense. I guess I get excited and forget to listen.\nA: Totally get it. Your energy's a real asset, so don't lose that.\nB: Thanks. Could you give me a nudge if ________?\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. I didn't realize __I was doing that__.\na. it came across that way\nb. it was a problem\nc. anyone had noticed\n\n2. I appreciate you __being upfront about it__.\na. pointing it out\nb. raising it with me\nc. being so honest\n\n3. Could you give me a nudge if __I slip up__?\na. I start doing it again\nb. I get carried away\nc. I cut someone off\n",
