     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 6 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 8, 10, 11\nFergus and Georgia are leaving a talk on AI and jobs.\nFergus: Well, that was cheery. Apparently half of us will be replaced by robots.\nGeorgia: **I'd argue** that's a bit alarmist. AI changes jobs more than it kills them.\nFergus: Tell that to translators. Or illustrators.\nGeorgia: True, they're getting hit hard. **On the flip side**, whole new roles are popping up.\nFergus: Sure, but can a fifty-year-old translator just retrain overnight?\nGeorgia: Not overnight, no. That's where governments and employers need to step up.\nFergus: Mate, I wouldn't hold my breath.\nGeorgia: Cynic! But really, **it boils down to** how we use it.\nFergus: Or who gets to own it. That's the real question, I reckon.\nGeorgia: Okay, that one calls for a drink. You're buying.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 9\n1. Mate, I wouldn't hold my breath.\nchange: “hold my” (mất âm d)\nstrong: “Mate”, “wouldn't”, “breath”\nGiọng Úc thường đọc /eɪ/ gần như “ai”: “Mate” nghe như “mait”. “hold my” → “hôl-mai”. Giọng hoài nghi (ý: đừng mong), xuống ở cuối.\n\n2. I'd argue that's a bit alarmist.\nlinking: “I'd‿argue”, “that's‿a”\nchange: “bit‿alarmist” (t → d nhẹ)\nstrong: “argue”, “alarmist”\n“I'd argue” → “ai-đar-giu”; giọng Mỹ: “bit alarmist” → “bi-đơ-lar-mịst”. “a bit” làm lời phản bác mềm hơn.\n\n3. On the flip side, whole new roles are popping up.\nlinking: “popping‿up”\nweak: “the”, “are”\nstrong: “flip side”, “whole new roles”\n“popping up” nối thành “pá-pi-ngắp”. Ngắt nhẹ sau “On the flip side”, rồi nhấn “whole new roles” vì đó là ý mới.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nGiọng Úc thường đọc /eɪ/ gần “ai” (mate, day) và không đọc /r/ sau nguyên âm (translator, overnight).\nGiọng Mỹ: t giữa hai nguyên âm, kể cả giữa hai từ, thành “d” nhẹ: bit alarmist.\nCâu mỉa mai (Well, that was cheery.) đọc giọng đều, kéo dài rồi xuống thấp.\nKhi tranh luận, ngắt nhẹ sau cụm mở đầu (I'd argue, On the flip side) rồi nhấn vào ý chính.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**Tell that to translators.**\nThử nói câu đó với dân dịch thuật xem.\n“Tell that to + ai đó” = phản bác: những người đó sẽ không đồng ý với bạn đâu.\nCách nói tương đương: Translators would beg to differ.\n\n**That's where governments and employers need to step up.**\nĐó là lúc chính phủ và giới chủ phải vào cuộc.\n“step up” = đứng ra nhận trách nhiệm, hành động khi cần. “That's where…” = đó chính là chỗ, là lúc…\nCách nói tương đương: That's where governments and employers come in.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nNêu lập luận: I'd argue (that)… / It boils down to…\nI'd argue (that) nêu quan điểm chắc chắn mà vẫn lịch sự. It boils down to + danh từ / mệnh đề = rốt cuộc, mấu chốt là…\n[[I'd argue that]] social media does more harm than good.\nIn the end, [[it boils down to]] money.\n[[It all comes down to]] who you know.\n\nXét mặt khác: On the flip side… / Then again…\nĐưa ra mặt ngược lại của vấn đề vừa nói. Then again = nhưng nghĩ lại thì…, dùng khi tự cân nhắc ý của chính mình.\nRemote work saves time. [[On the flip side]], it can feel lonely.\nCities are expensive. [[Then again]], salaries are higher.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 13\nA: Well, that was cheery. Apparently half of us will be replaced by robots.\nB: I'd argue that's ________. AI changes jobs more than it kills them.\nA: Tell that to translators. Or illustrators.\nB: True, they're getting hit hard. On the flip side, ________ are popping up.\nA: Sure, but can a fifty-year-old translator just retrain overnight?\nB: Not overnight, no. That's where governments and employers need to step up.\nA: Mate, I wouldn't hold my breath.\nB: Cynic! But really, it boils down to ________.\nA: Or who gets to own it. That's the real question, I reckon.\nB: Okay, that one calls for a drink. You're buying.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 14\n1. I'd argue that's __a bit alarmist__.\na. a bit simplistic\nb. an overreaction\nc. too pessimistic\n\n2. On the flip side, __whole new roles__ are popping up.\na. new industries\nb. all kinds of new jobs\nc. fresh opportunities\n\n3. But really, it boils down to __how we use it__.\na. how we regulate it\nb. education and training\nc. the choices we make\n",
