     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 7 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nNgan and Phuc are at a Dublin pub after a long week.\nNgan: Honestly, I'm **wrecked**. That presentation nearly killed me, so it did.\nPhuc: You smashed it, though. The boss was **kinda** blown away.\nNgan: Ah, stop. I nearly threw up beforehand. Right, what are you having?\nPhuc: Just a lemonade, thanks. I'm driving, and I'm **knackered**.\nNgan: Fair enough. **Wanna** split some chips? My treat.\nPhuc: Go on, then. Cheers. So, got any plans for the weekend?\nNgan: Nothing much. I'm **gonna** binge that new crime series.\nPhuc: Oh, it's **dead** good. Not **gonna** lie, the ending's absolutely mental.\nNgan: Don't you dare spoil it! Not another word, or you're paying.\nPhuc: My lips are sealed. Actually, I'll get these. You've earned it.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. The boss was kinda blown away.\nlinking: “blown‿away”\nweak: “was”\nstrong: “boss”, “blown away”\n“kinda” = kind of: “kai-nđơ”. “blown away” → “blâu-nơ-wây”. Giọng Anh đọc “boss” tròn môi /bɒs/; giọng Mỹ mở miệng hơn: “bas”.\n\n2. Not gonna lie, the ending's absolutely mental.\nchange: “Not gonna” (t thành âm tắc ở họng)\nweak: “the”\nstrong: “absolutely”, “mental”\nNgười Anh hay thay /t/ trước phụ âm bằng một khoảng ngắt ở họng: “no' gơ-nơ”. “absolutely” nhấn âm “lút”: /ˌæbsəˈluːtli/.\n\n3. Don't you dare spoil it! Not another word, or you're paying.\nchange: “Don't‿you” (t + y → “ch”)\nstrong: “dare”, “word”, “paying”\nGiọng Ireland đọc rõ /r/ sau nguyên âm (dare, word, or), giọng Anh thì không. Nhấn “dare”, giọng doạ mà vui.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\ngonna, wanna, kinda đọc “gơ-nơ”, “wa-nơ”, “kai-nđơ”; chỉ dùng khi nói hoặc nhắn tin thân mật.\nNgười Anh hay thay /t/ trước phụ âm bằng âm tắc ở họng: not gonna → “no' gơ-nơ”.\nGiọng Ireland đọc rõ /r/ sau nguyên âm (dare, word); giọng Anh thì không.\nNói tiếng lóng với giọng thoải mái, dồn trọng âm vào từ lóng: knackered, mental.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**That presentation nearly killed me, so it did.**\nBài thuyết trình đó suýt lấy mạng tôi, thật đấy.\n“nearly killed me” là nói quá (cực kỳ vất vả). Thêm đuôi “so + chủ ngữ + trợ động từ” (so it did, so I am) để nhấn mạnh là nét quen thuộc của người Ireland.\nCách nói tương đương: That presentation really took it out of me.\n\n**My lips are sealed.**\nTôi sẽ không hé răng nửa lời.\nHứa giữ bí mật, không tiết lộ gì (ở đây: không kể đoạn kết phim).\nCách nói tương đương: I won't say a word.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nRút gọn khi nói nhanh: gonna / wanna / kinda\ngonna = going to + động từ (không thay “going to” + nơi chốn), wanna = want to, kinda = kind of (hơi, khá là). Chỉ dùng khi nói hoặc nhắn tin thân mật.\nI'm [[gonna]] crash early tonight.\nDo you [[wanna]] grab a bite?\nIt's [[kinda]] cold in here.\n\nTừ lóng tả cảm giác: wrecked / knackered / dead + tính từ\nwrecked, knackered = mệt rã rời (Anh, Ireland); người Mỹ hay nói I'm beat. dead + tính từ = rất (dead good, dead easy).\nI'm [[knackered]]. I've been up since five.\nThat quiz was [[dead easy]].\nI'm [[beat]]. Let's call it a night.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: Honestly, I'm wrecked. That presentation nearly killed me, so it did.\nB: You ________, though. The boss was kinda blown away.\nA: Ah, stop. I nearly threw up beforehand. Right, what are you having?\nB: Just a lemonade, thanks. I'm driving, and I'm ________.\nA: Fair enough. Wanna split some chips? My treat.\nB: Go on, then. Cheers. So, got any plans for the weekend?\nA: Nothing much. I'm gonna binge that new crime series.\nB: Oh, it's dead good. Not gonna lie, the ending's absolutely ________.\nA: Don't you dare spoil it! Not another word, or you're paying.\nB: My lips are sealed. Actually, I'll get these. You've earned it.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. You __smashed it__, though.\na. nailed it\nb. killed it\nc. totally aced it\n\n2. I'm driving, and I'm __knackered__.\na. shattered\nb. dead on my feet\nc. running on empty\n\n3. Not gonna lie, the ending's absolutely __mental__.\na. insane\nb. unreal\nc. wild\n",
