     "md": "Level 10/unit 8/unit 8.md",
     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 8 — CD2\n\n[1] Conversation — track 22, 24, 25\nGareth and Helena have just heard that their company is restructuring.\nGareth: Well, that was a bombshell, eh? Our whole department's **up in the air**.\nHelena: Seriously. And with the merger falling through, we're **back to square one**.\nGareth: Do you reckon they'll **lay people off**?\nHelena: They didn't **rule it out**. That's what worries me.\nGareth: Same. If you read between the lines, it's all about cutting costs.\nHelena: Probably. Either way, **the ball's in their court** now.\nGareth: True. Still, I might dust off my CV, just in case.\nHelena: Smart move. I'm gonna keep my head down and see how it **plays out**.\nGareth: Fancy a coffee? I need to get my head around all this.\nHelena: Sure, but no shop talk. My brain's completely fried.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 23\n1. Well, that was a bombshell, eh?\nlinking: “was‿a”\nweak: “was”, “a”\nstrong: “bombshell”, “eh”\n“eh” cuối câu là nét rất New Zealand, giống “nhỉ”: đọc “ây” và lên giọng để tìm sự đồng tình.\n\n2. And with the merger falling through, we're back to square one.\nsmooth: “back to square one”\nweak: “the”, “to”\nstrong: “falling through”, “square one”\nỞ tốc độ thật, “back to square one” đọc liền một hơi: “bác-tơ-squer-wăn”. Giọng Mỹ đọc rõ /r/ trong “merger”, “square”.\n\n3. Do you reckon they'll lay people off?\nsmooth: “Do you”\nlinking: “people‿off”\nstrong: “reckon”, “off”\n“Do you” lướt thành “đơ-yơ”; “people off” → “pi-pơ-lóf”. Giọng New Zealand thường đọc /e/ gần “i”: “reckon” nghe như “rí-cần”.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nGiọng New Zealand thường đọc /e/ gần “i” (reckon), /æ/ gần “e” (Fancy); cuối câu hay có “eh?” lên giọng.\nThành ngữ ở tốc độ thật đọc liền như một từ: back to square one, the ball's in their court.\nPhrasal verb đứng cuối câu thường nhấn vào tiểu từ: lay people OFF, rule it OUT, plays OUT.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**If you read between the lines, it's all about cutting costs.**\nĐọc kỹ ý tứ thì rốt cuộc là chuyện cắt giảm chi phí.\n“read between the lines” = hiểu ý ngầm, điều người ta không nói thẳng ra.\nCách nói tương đương: The hidden agenda is cutting costs.\n\n**I need to get my head around all this.**\nTôi cần tiêu hoá hết mấy chuyện này đã.\n“get your head around something” = hiểu, chấp nhận được một điều phức tạp hoặc bất ngờ.\nCách nói tương đương: I need time to process all this.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nThành ngữ khi tình hình chưa rõ ràng\nup in the air = chưa quyết, chưa rõ; back to square one = quay về vạch xuất phát; the ball's in someone's court = đến lượt ai đó quyết định.\nOur holiday plans are still [[up in the air]].\nThe deal collapsed, so it's [[back to square one]].\nI've made my offer. [[The ball's in your court]].\n\nPhrasal verbs trong tin công ty: lay off / rule out / play out\nlay off = cho nghỉ việc (vì cắt giảm); rule out = loại trừ một khả năng; play out = diễn biến, xảy ra.\nThe factory [[laid off]] two hundred workers.\nDoctors haven't [[ruled out]] surgery.\nLet's wait and see how things [[play out]].\n\n[5] Role Play — track 27\nA: Well, that was a bombshell, eh? Our whole department's up in the air.\nB: Seriously. And with the merger falling through, we're ________.\nA: Do you reckon they'll lay people off?\nB: They didn't rule it out. That's what worries me.\nA: Same. If you read between the lines, it's all about cutting costs.\nB: Probably. Either way, ________ now.\nA: True. Still, I might dust off my CV, just in case.\nB: Smart move. I'm gonna keep my head down and see how it ________.\nA: Fancy a coffee? I need to get my head around all this.\nB: Sure, but no shop talk. My brain's completely fried.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 28\n1. And with the merger falling through, we're __back to square one__.\na. starting from scratch\nb. back where we started\nc. in limbo again\n\n2. Either way, __the ball's in their court__ now.\na. it's out of our hands\nb. it's their call\nc. it's up to management\n\n3. I'm gonna keep my head down and see how it __plays out__.\na. pans out\nb. unfolds\nc. shakes out\n",
