     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 9 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 1, 3, 4\nThang is just back from a road trip in Queensland. Juliet wants to hear all about it.\nJuliet: So, how was the road trip? Any drama?\nThang: Oh, you have no idea. **So there I was**, driving along the coast at night.\nJuliet: Oh dear. I don't like where this is going.\nThang: **Out of nowhere**, something huge and hairy drops onto my shoulder.\nJuliet: No way. Please tell me it wasn't a huntsman.\nThang: It was. **I thought to myself**, okay, stay calm, don't crash the car.\nJuliet: Good call. So what did you do?\nThang: Pulled over, jumped out, slammed the door. Then **it hit me**. My phone was still inside.\nJuliet: With the spider? Mate, you could've just shooed it out!\nThang: You weren't there! **I was like**, nope, that's its car now.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 2\n1. So there I was, driving along the coast at night.\nlinking: “there‿I”, “coast‿at”\nstrong: “was”, “coast”, “night”\nGiọng Mỹ nối /r/: “there I” → “đhe-rai”. “was” cuối cụm đọc mạnh /wʌz/. Chậm lại và ngắt một nhịp sau “was” để tạo hồi hộp.\n\n2. Out of nowhere, something huge and hairy drops onto my shoulder.\nchange: “Out‿of” (t → d nhẹ)\nweak: “and”, “my”\nstrong: “huge”, “hairy”, “shoulder”\n“Out of” → “ao-đơv”. Nhấn “huge”, “hairy” và nói nhanh dần, như đang sống lại khoảnh khắc đó.\n\n3. With the spider? Mate, you could've just shooed it out!\nchange: “could've” (have → “ơv”)\nlinking: “shooed‿it‿out”\nstrong: “spider”, “shooed”\n“could've” → “cu-đơv”; “shooed it out” → “shu-đi-đao”. Giọng Úc không đọc /r/ cuối “spider”. Lên giọng ở “spider?” vì không tin nổi.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nKhi kể chuyện, chậm lại lúc dựng cảnh (So there I was…), rồi nói nhanh dần ở đoạn gay cấn.\nNgắt một nhịp trước chi tiết bất ngờ: Then it hit me. (ngắt) My phone was still inside.\n“was” cuối cụm đọc mạnh /wʌz/; giữa câu đọc yếu /wəz/.\nGiọng Mỹ và giọng Úc đều hay đọc t giữa hai nguyên âm thành “d” nhẹ: out of, shooed it out.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**I don't like where this is going.**\nNghe có vẻ không ổn rồi đây.\nPhản ứng của người nghe khi đoán câu chuyện sắp có biến; giúp người kể thêm hào hứng.\nCách nói tương đương: This doesn't sound good.\n\n**Oh, you have no idea.**\nÔi, cậu không tưởng tượng nổi đâu.\nCâu mở màn trước khi kể một chuyện ly kỳ, khiến người nghe tò mò muốn nghe tiếp.\nCách nói tương đương: Where do I even start?\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nTạo hồi hộp: So there I was… / Out of nowhere… / Then it hit me\nSo there I was dựng cảnh; out of nowhere báo điều bất ngờ; then it hit me = chợt nhận ra. Có thể chuyển sang thì hiện tại cho sống động.\n[[So there I was]], stuck in a lift alone.\n[[Out of nowhere]], the lights went off.\n[[Then it hit me]]. I'd left the oven on.\n\nKể lại suy nghĩ: I thought to myself… / I was like…\nThuật lại suy nghĩ, phản ứng như lời nói trực tiếp, không lùi thì. I was like… rất thân mật, chỉ dùng khi nói.\n[[I thought to myself]], this can't be happening.\nHe asked me to sing, and [[I was like]], no way!\n\n[5] Role Play — track 6\nA: So, how was the road trip? Any drama?\nB: Oh, you have no idea. So there I was, ________.\nA: Oh dear. I don't like where this is going.\nB: Out of nowhere, something huge and hairy drops onto my shoulder.\nA: No way. Please tell me it wasn't a huntsman.\nB: It was. I thought to myself, okay, ________, don't crash the car.\nA: Good call. So what did you do?\nB: Pulled over, jumped out, slammed the door. Then it hit me. My phone was still inside.\nA: With the spider? Mate, you could've just shooed it out!\nB: You weren't there! I was like, nope, ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 7\n1. So there I was, __driving along the coast at night__.\na. half asleep at the wheel\nb. miles from the nearest town\nc. singing along to the radio\n\n2. I thought to myself, okay, __stay calm__, don't crash the car.\na. deep breaths\nb. don't panic\nc. keep it together\n\n3. I was like, nope, __that's its car now__.\na. I'm walking home\nb. I'm not getting back in\nc. it can keep the car\n",
