     "mdText": "[HEADER] unit 11 — CD3\n\n[1] Conversation — track 15, 17, 18\nQuynh is flying home to Vietnam for Tet. Her colleague Lionel is curious.\nLionel: So Tet is basically Vietnamese Christmas, right?\nQuynh: Sort of. **It's a bit like** Christmas and New Year rolled into one.\nLionel: Okay, so what does everyone actually do?\nQuynh: **Traditionally**, we clean the whole house beforehand. But during Tet itself, no sweeping.\nLionel: Wait, why not?\nQuynh: **It's considered** bad luck. You'd be sweeping your good fortune out the door!\nLionel: Love it. And presents? We go a bit overboard at Christmas.\nQuynh: Not so much. **It's customary to** give kids lucky money in red envelopes.\nLionel: Cash instead of socks? Those kids have it all figured out.\nQuynh: Exactly! Oh, and the first guest of the year matters. **The idea is that** they set the tone.\n\n[2] Speak Like a Native — track 16\n1. It's a bit like Christmas and New Year rolled into one.\nlinking: “rolled‿into‿one”\nweak: “a”, “and”\nstrong: “Christmas”, “New Year”, “one”\nChữ t trong “Christmas” câm: “kris-mơs”. “rolled into one” → “rôl-đin-tu-wăn”. Giọng New Zealand không đọc /r/ cuối “Year”: “yia”.\n\n2. You'd be sweeping your good fortune out the door!\nchange: “You'd be” (mất âm d)\nweak: “your”, “the”\nstrong: “sweeping”, “good fortune”, “door”\n“fortune” /ˈfɔːtʃuːn/ đọc “fo-chun”. Giọng New Zealand không đọc /r/ trong “fortune”, “door”. Giọng vui, hơi cường điệu.\n\n3. Cash instead of socks? Those kids have it all figured out.\nlinking: “instead‿of”, “have‿it‿all”, “figured‿out”\nstrong: “Cash”, “socks”, “figured out”\nGiọng Mỹ: “have it all” → “ha-vi-đol” (t → d nhẹ), “figured out” → “fi-gyơr-đao”. Lên giọng ở “socks?” vì thích thú.\n\n[MẸO PHÁT ÂM]\nChữ t câm trong Christmas, listen, castle: “kris-mơs”, “li-sần”, “ca-sồ”.\nGiọng New Zealand không đọc /r/ cuối (year, door); giọng Mỹ đọc rõ (figured, overboard).\nKhi giải thích phong tục, nói chậm và nhấn từ khoá: bad luck, lucky money, first guest.\nNối các từ ngắn thành cụm: rolled‿into‿one, have‿it‿all.\n\n[3] Study Notes\n**We go a bit overboard at Christmas.**\nNhà tôi mua sắm hơi quá tay vào dịp Giáng sinh.\n“go overboard” = làm quá đà (mua sắm, trang trí, ăn uống…).\nCách nói tương đương: We tend to overdo it at Christmas.\n\n**Those kids have it all figured out.**\nMấy đứa nhỏ đó đúng là biết tính.\n“have it all figured out” = hiểu rõ, tính toán đâu ra đấy. Lionel nói đùa: tiền mặt hơn hẳn đôi tất.\nCách nói tương đương: Those kids are onto something.\n\n[4] Grammar Focus\nMô tả phong tục: Traditionally, … / It's customary to + V\nTraditionally = theo truyền thống; It's customary to + V = theo phong tục thì làm gì (trang trọng hơn “people usually…”).\n[[Traditionally]], the whole family eats together on New Year's Eve.\n[[It's customary to]] take your shoes off indoors.\n\nGiải thích ý nghĩa: It's considered… / The idea is that… / It's a bit like…\nIt's considered + tính từ / danh từ: quan niệm chung. The idea is that: giải thích lý do. It's a bit like: so sánh với điều người nghe đã biết.\n[[It's considered]] rude to point at people.\n[[The idea is that]] red keeps bad luck away.\n[[It's a bit like]] Thanksgiving, but longer.\n\n[5] Role Play — track 20\nA: So Tet is basically Vietnamese Christmas, right?\nB: Sort of. It's a bit like ________ rolled into one.\nA: Okay, so what does everyone actually do?\nB: Traditionally, we ________ beforehand. But during Tet itself, no sweeping.\nA: Wait, why not?\nB: It's considered bad luck. You'd be sweeping your good fortune out the door!\nA: Love it. And presents? We go a bit overboard at Christmas.\nB: Not so much. It's customary to give kids lucky money in red envelopes.\nA: Cash instead of socks? Those kids have it all figured out.\nB: Exactly! Oh, and the first guest of the year matters. The idea is that they ________.\n\n[6] Substitution Drill — track 21\n1. It's a bit like __Christmas and New Year__ rolled into one.\na. Thanksgiving and New Year\nb. a reunion and a festival\nc. a holiday and a birthday\n\n2. Traditionally, we __clean the whole house__ beforehand.\na. pay off our debts\nb. visit our ancestors' graves\nc. buy peach blossoms\n\n3. The idea is that they __set the tone__.\na. bring good luck\nb. decide your fortune\nc. shape the whole year\n",
